o close military outposts in Tunisia, Cameroon, Libya and Kenya.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Pentagon is considering withdrawing nearly all American commandos from Niger in the wake of a deadly October ambush that killed four United States soldiers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/01/us/politics/00dc-military/merlin_136996785_7099728c-0924-4817-9153-8f6bd735d798-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/01/us/politics/00dc-military/merlin_136996785_7099728c-0924-4817-9153-8f6bd735d798-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/01/us/politics/00dc-military/merlin_136996785_7099728c-0924-4817-9153-8f6bd735d798-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/01/us/politics/00dc-military/merlin_136996785_7099728c-0924-4817-9153-8f6bd735d798-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/01/us/politics/00dc-military/00dc-military-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/01/us/politics/00dc-military/00dc-military-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/01/us/politics/00dc-military/00dc-military-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Deadly Raid, Pentagon Weighs Withdrawing Almost All Commandos From Niger', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Deaths, U.S. Weighs Withdrawing Commandos From Niger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Africa Command', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Special Operations Command', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army Special Forces (Green Berets)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mattis, James N', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldhauser, Thomas D', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-02T14:31:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Gibbons-Neff and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gibbons-Neff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54f4a28a-b805-54a3-bd41-d8c6e693520f', 'word_count': 1044, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54f4a28a-b805-54a3-bd41-d8c6e693520f'}, {'abstract': 'Seven alumni died in 2016, then 13 more the next year. How could any school, even one for troubled youths, have so many of its students die so young?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nyt