 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/02/opinion/rohingya-genocide-myanmar-united-nations.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations condemns Myanmar’s generals but takes no tangible steps toward punishment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Officials with the United Nations and other international bodies have offered no action plan after the organization delivered a report that found Myanmar’s army systematically slaughtered the Rohingya Mulims last year. More than 700,000 people were driven from their homes during a campaign of mass murder and rape, the investigation found.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/03/opinion/03heng-inyt/03heng-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/03/opinion/03heng-inyt/03heng-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/03/opinion/03heng-inyt/03heng-inyt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/03/opinion/03heng-inyt/03heng-inyt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1489, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/03/opinion/03heng-inyt/03heng-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/03/opinion/03heng-inyt/03heng-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/03/opinion/03heng-inyt/03heng-inyt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rohingya Hurry Up and Wait for Justice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rohingya (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-02T20:06:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heng', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heng', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c49baaae-f4c9-5c3c-9c57-b2d3ea84a71c', 'word_count': 69, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c49baaae-f4c9-5c3c-9c57-b2d3ea84a71c'}, {'abstract': 'Most confirmation hearings concern nominees who would not change the court’s basic direction. Judge Kavanaugh is the rare nominee who would, for two important reasons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/02/us/politics/judge-kavanaugh-supreme-court-justices.html', 'snippet': 'Most confirmation hearings concern nominees who would not change the court’s basic direction. Judge Kavanaugh is the rare nominee who would, for two important reasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Most Supreme Court appointments are in a way inconsequential. A conservative replaces a conservative, a liberal replaces a liberal, and the court’s basic direction is unchanged.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', '