17536-5f05-5765-9058-3b4b7f75e0cc'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on how DNA undoes secrecy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/03/magazine/can-i-tell-my-brother-the-truth-about-our-paternity.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on how DNA undoes secrecy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m 45, living in the United States. My brother is two years older and lives in Australia. Neither of us gets on with our 86-year-old mother, who lives in London. Our father, whom we were both really close to, died in 1985 after a long illness. I was 13, my brother 15, and it affected us very badly with little help from our mother.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-ethicist-image1/09mag-ethicist-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-ethicist-image1/09mag-ethicist-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 601}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-ethicist-image1/09mag-ethicist-image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-ethicist-image1/09mag-ethicist-image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1201, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-ethicist-image1/09mag-ethicist-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-ethicist-image1/09mag-ethicist-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-ethicist-image1/09mag-ethicist-image1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can I Tell My Brother the Truth About Our Paternity?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can I Tell My Brother the Truth About Our Paternity?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '23andMe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-04T02:25:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d579eb80-7fb1-5082-a089-92ac6a529871', 'word_count': 1729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d579eb80-7fb1-5082-a089-92ac6a529871'}, {'abstract': 'A masterful balance between sweet and tart, crunch and tenderness from a small restaurant in Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/03/magazine/chocolate-chip-cookie-cranberry-paris.html', 'snippet': 'A masterful balance between sweet and tart, crunch and tenderness from a small restaurant in Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It takes me forever to get anywhere in Paris. It’s not the traffic, or the strikes — which are almost as reliable as the church bells tolling the hours — or the weather, or the bumpy cobblestone streets. It’s the pastry shops: There are so many of them, and I can’t keep myself from lingering in front of their windows. I’ve been stopped hundreds of times by the sight of cakes and tarts, small pastries of all shapes, cannelés browned to a burned-sugar patina and colorful macarons, of course. I’m an easy mark when it comes to sweets, which is why it’s odd that in my decades-long wanderings I’ve stopped for cookies only once. And that time, they weren’t even in a patisserie.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-OnDessert-image1/09mag-OnDessert-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 414, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-OnDessert-image1/09mag-OnDessert-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 414}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-OnDessert-image1/09mag-OnDessert-image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-OnDessert-image1/09mag-OnDessert-image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1412, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-OnDessert-image1/09mag-OnDessert-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-OnDessert-image1/09mag-OnDessert-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09mag-OnDessert-image1/09mag-OnDessert-image1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Elevate Your Chocolate-Chip Cookies', 'kicker': 'On Dessert', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beyond the Chocolate-Chip Cookie', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mokonuts (Paris, France, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-04T02:25:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorie Greenspan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenspan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/092f9fcf-373c-56bd-b62d-301e3a13b775', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/092f9fcf-373c-56bd-b62d-301e3a13b775'}, {'abstract': 'Make rules. Make sure seven or eight people show up. Go for two hours.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/03/magazine/how-to-start-a-book-group.html', 'snippet': 'Make rules. Make sure seven or eight people show up. Go for two hours.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s important to have a set of rules, even if over time they kind of disintegrate,” says David Peplow, a senior lecturer at Sheffield Hallam University in England who has done multiyear ethnographies of book groups. Make your guiding principles answer basic questions: What kind of books will you read? How will books be chosen? Where will you meet? How will you make sure everyone who wants to talk gets a chance to? Peplow believes that literary fiction and memoirs tend to prompt the most engaged conversations.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09Mag-Tip-1/09Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09Mag-Tip-1/09Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 527}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09Mag-Tip-1/09Mag-Tip-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09Mag-Tip-1/09Mag-Tip-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1798, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09Mag-Tip-1/09Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09Mag-Tip-1/09Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/magazine/09Mag-Tip-1/09Mag-Tip-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thu