sberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fda99a6-7286-56f9-8a62-ae38e20ecc9f', 'word_count': 1398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fda99a6-7286-56f9-8a62-ae38e20ecc9f'}, {'abstract': 'The chef Fany Gerson’s holiday feast is born of her Jewish heritage and Mexico City upbringing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/04/dining/mexican-recipes-rosh-hashanah-fany-gerson.html', 'snippet': 'The chef Fany Gerson’s holiday feast is born of her Jewish heritage and Mexico City upbringing.', 'lead_paragraph': "In the late 1920s, the chef Fany Gerson’s grandparents, Jewish and facing persecution, fled Ukraine and boarded boats bound for New York City. But they weren't able to immigrate through Ellis Island, for reasons they can't quite remember — perhaps because of financial turmoil preceding the 1929 stock market crash, or because of limits set a few years earlier on the number of immigrants from certain countries. ", 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05fany5/merlin_141928068_6c46b3da-83e0-44f7-a70e-7545c1766fd7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05fany5/merlin_141928068_6c46b3da-83e0-44f7-a70e-7545c1766fd7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05fany5/merlin_141928068_6c46b3da-83e0-44f7-a70e-7545c1766fd7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05fany5/merlin_141928068_6c46b3da-83e0-44f7-a70e-7545c1766fd7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05fany5/05fany5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05fany5/05fany5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05fany5/05fany5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Matzo Balls and Chiles? It’s Rosh Hashana With the Flavors of Mexico', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Flavors of Mexico Come Home for Rosh Hashana', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rosh Hashana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mexican Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'La Newyorkina (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gerson, Fany', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico City (Mexico)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-04T17:23:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Priya Krishna', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Priya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krishna', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ccd3c4b-8f77-519c-b0d3-b9796c0f181f', 'word_count': 1160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ccd3c4b-8f77-519c-b0d3-b9796c0f181f'}, {'abstract': 'Ambitious fare with an elegant accent in NoMad, seafood on the Upper West Side, chef moves and other restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/04/dining/nyc-restaurant-news.html', 'snippet': 'Ambitious fare with an elegant accent in NoMad, seafood on the Upper West Side, chef moves and other restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yakitori — grilled, skewered chicken tidbits — is the Japanese food of the moment in New York, with new places like Nonono opening at a steady clip. It is usually considered casual pub-style izakaya food, but at Toriko NY, a West Village branch of a collection of restaurants in Tokyo and Osaka, it becomes carefully orchestrated multicourse omakase fare. (For $85, there are starters, 10 courses of yakitori, a final bowl of ramen or rice, and dessert; in a few weeks, there will also be an à la carte menu.) Top quality ingredients like Bo Bo chickens and Miyazaki Wagyu from Japan are used, and there’s a well-designed wine list, mostly French. A counter that seats 19 surrounds the central open kitchen, where affable chefs trim, skewer, grill and season pieces of drumstick, gizzards, chicken breast and the like. There are also about 20 seats at tables on the perimeter of the restaurant, done in honeyed polished wood and stone. The group that has brought Toriko to New York also owns Mifune New York and Sushi Amane here.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05Off1/merlin_142989825_c586ea4a-65cb-4ba1-aa41-2a23ce718a05-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05Off1/merlin_142989825_c586ea4a-65cb-4ba1-aa41-2a23ce718a05-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05Off1/merlin_142989825_c586ea4a-65cb-4ba1-aa41-2a23ce718a05-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05Off1/merlin_142989825_c586ea4a-65cb-4ba1-aa41-2a23ce718a05-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05Off1/05Off1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05Off1/05Off1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/dining/05Off1/05Off1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Elevated Yakitori, Direct From Japan, in the West Village', 'kicker': 'Off the menu', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Joseph (JJ) (1984- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burke, David (1962- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Dwyane (1982- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-04T17:27:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33129282-2d5d-54ea-b9d4-6ba2b49964d3', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33129282-2d5d-54ea-b9d4-6ba2b49964d3'}, {'abstract': 'The threat of Donald Trump and new pressure from reformers are likely to summon his formidable strengths.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/04/opinion/cuomo-governor-endorsement-new-york-times.html', 'snippet': 'The threat of Donald Trump and new pressure from reformers are likely to summon his formidable strengths.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York is a big state with small politics. It is home to many of the most ambitious and inventive people in the world, but its governance is stunted by party hacks and special interests, petty rivalries and systemic corruption.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/04/opinion/04andrewWeb/04andrewWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/04/opinion/04andrewWeb/04andrewWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 757}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/04/opinion/04andrewWeb/04andrewWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 812, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/04/opinion/04andrewWeb/04andrewWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1623, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima