may be on the horizon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The reports this week that the Alley Oop comic strip was on its deathbed may have been premature. Its current creative team signed off in a strip on Saturday for the comic, which debuted on Dec. 5, 1932, but in an interview, John Glynn, president and editorial director of the company that distributes Alley Oop, hinted at a possible future.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/arts/05arts3/05alleyoop-item-articleLarge.png', 'height': 182, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/05/arts/05arts3/05alleyoop-item-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 182}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/arts/05arts3/05alleyoop-item-jumbo.png', 'height': 281, 'width': 926, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/arts/05arts3/05alleyoop-item-superJumbo.png', 'height': 281, 'width': 926, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/arts/05arts3/05alleyoop-item-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/05/arts/05arts3/05alleyoop-item-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/arts/05arts3/05alleyoop-item-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alley Oo