0fc29412f'}, {'abstract': 'Twenty years after the publication of her memoir about her relationship with J.D. Salinger, Joyce Maynard revisits the book’s vicious reception.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/05/books/review/joyce-maynard-at-home-in-the-world.html', 'snippet': 'Twenty years after the publication of her memoir about her relationship with J.D. Salinger, Joyce Maynard revisits the book’s vicious reception.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been said of me, in the pages of this newspaper, that I am a predator. The author of those words was hardly alone in her assessment. In 1998, nearly 20 years before the #MeToo movement, I published a book about my relationship with a famous and revered writer who sought me out when he was 53 and I was 18.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09Maynard1-sub/09Maynard1-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 542, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09Maynard1-sub/09Maynard1-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 542}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09Maynard1-sub/09Maynard1-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 925, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09Maynard1-sub/09Maynard1-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1850, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09Maynard1-sub/09Maynard1-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09Maynard1-sub/09Maynard1-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09Maynard1-sub/09Maynard1-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Was She J.D. Salinger’s Predator or His Prey?', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Me, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'At Home in the World (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maynard, Joyce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '#MeToo Movement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-05T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Maynard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maynard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/427f9ac5-73f6-5974-a233-5387408685e6', 'word_count': 1508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/427f9ac5-73f6-5974-a233-5387408685e6'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/05/books/review/new-noteworthy-james-ryerson.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jane Austen — that most enduringly popular of early-19th-century writers, chronicler of domesticity and love — gets the star treatment yet again in new recordings of two of her most famous novels: SENSE AND SENSIBILITY, read by Rosamund Pike, and EMMA, read by Emma Thompson and a cast including Joanne Froggat and Morgana Robinson. (Audible Studios.) SADIE By Courtney Summers. Read by a full cast including Rebecca Soler, Fred Berman, Dan Bittner and Gabra Zackman. (Macmillan Audio.) A girl searching for her sister’s killer employs the help of a radio personality who turns her quest for justice into a podcast. The premise of this young adult thriller makes it a perfect audiobook, as much of the story is recounted as a radio whodunit. CORDUROY TAKES A BOW By Viola Davis. Read by the author. (Listening Library.) As the lovable teddy bear Corduroy turns 50, the award-winning actress takes over as author of this classic children’s book series, delivering a fitting story about Corduroy’s first visit to the theater. For young listeners new to audiobooks, Davis’s reading makes for an excellent gateway to future listening. THE BELOVED WORLD OF SONIA SOTOMAYOR By Sonia Sotomayor. Read by Jaina Lee Ortiz, with an introduction read by the author. (Listening Library.) The Supreme Court justice tells the story of her life in this middle-grade version of her best-selling adult memoir, “My Beloved World.” From growing up in the rough housing projects of the South Bronx to dealing with juvenile diabetes and her parents’ financial troubles, this is a story about overcoming adversity and achieving the seemingly impossible.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09NewNoteworthy0/09NewNoteworthy0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 200, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09NewNoteworthy0/09NewNoteworthy0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 200}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09NewNoteworthy0/09NewNoteworthy0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09NewNoteworthy0/09NewNoteworthy0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 1823, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09NewNoteworthy0/09NewNoteworthy0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09NewNoteworthy0/09NewNoteworthy0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/books/review/09NewNoteworthy0/09NewNoteworthy0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New & Noteworthy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-05T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6eddf85-aae8-5fd5-9472-a151a7aaacf2', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6eddf85-aae8-5fd5-9472-a151a7aaacf2'}, {'abstract': 'Not many people have a good understanding of how Google delivers search results. And for good reason — the company tries to keep it a secret.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/05/technology/google-trump-bias.html', 'snippet': 'Not many people have a good understanding of how Google delivers search results. And for good reason — the company tries to keep it a secret.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Online search and Google are synonymous. About 90 percent of all searches on the web run through Google, giving the company an enormous role in directing the worldwide flow of information on the internet.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/business/06SEARCHQA.illoPRINT/merlin_143280078_c49b48a2-5990-444d-b45b-8508a97e1108-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 465, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/06/business/06SEARCHQA.illoPRINT/merlin_143280078_c49b48a2-5990-444d-b45b-8508a97e1108-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 465}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/business/06SEARCHQA.illoPRINT/merlin_143280078_c49b48a2-5990-444d-b45b-8508a97e1108-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 794, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/business/06SEARCHQA.illoPRINT/merlin_143280078_c49b48a2-5990-444d-b45b-8508a97e1108-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1588, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/business/06SEARCHQA.illoPRINT/merlin_143280078_c49b48a2-5990-444d-b45b-8508a97e1108-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/06/busines