superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09parking/09parking-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09parking/09parking-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09parking/09parking-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Double-Parking Savior of Public School 29', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Double-Parking Savior of P.S. 29', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public School 29 (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-06T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra E. Petri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Petri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2802a0b1-6685-5a65-9324-728200f77f44', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2802a0b1-6685-5a65-9324-728200f77f44'}, {'abstract': 'Decades after a killing, a man returns to post-apartheid corruption in his hometown in this picture by Michael Matthews.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/06/movies/five-fingers-for-marseilles-review.html', 'snippet': 'Decades after a killing, a man returns to post-apartheid corruption in his hometown in this picture by Michael Matthews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five teenage boys stand in a circle, each pointing a slingshot at the others. The camera follows their glances as they look to see who will betray the stillness. For fans of Sergio Leone, this setup may seem familiar, but the standoff takes place in compellingly undiscovered country, where the rule of genre is as malleable as the rule of the law.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07fivefingers/merlin_143157942_dce477e2-b655-48c7-bdc2-67793f0fd601-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07fivefingers/merlin_143157942_dce477e2-b655-48c7-bdc2-67793f0fd601-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07fivefingers/merlin_143157942_dce477e2-b655-48c7-bdc2-67793f0fd601-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07fivefingers/merlin_143157942_dce477e2-b655-48c7-bdc2-67793f0fd601-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07fivefingers/07fivefingers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07fivefingers/07fivefingers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07fivefingers/07fivefingers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Five Fingers for Marseilles’ Takes the Western to South Africa', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Five Fingers for Marseilles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Five Fingers for Marseilles (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matthews, Michael (Film Director)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-06T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teo Bugbee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bugbee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d44afdf-df90-5c40-a355-215952e04a0d', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d44afdf-df90-5c40-a355-215952e04a0d'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Hawke stepped behind the camera to tell the story of Blaze Foley, whose brief life was marked by love, whiskey, friendship, music and whiskey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/06/movies/blaze-review-ethan-hawke.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Hawke stepped behind the camera to tell the story of Blaze Foley, whose brief life was marked by love, whiskey, friendship, music and whiskey.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Blaze,” Ethan Hawke’s new movie (he directed, co-wrote the screenplay and appears onscreen a handful of times), whetted an appetite I wasn’t aware I had, though my Apple Music streaming history might have provided a clue. Even if the film were no good at all — and I’m relieved to say that it’s pretty darn good — I would be 100 percent here for a biopic about Blaze Foley, a Texas-based singer-songwriter who died in 1989. (His real name was Michael Fuller.) Furthermore, I would not be sad if “Blaze” kicked off a trend, and I could look forward to sad, smoky, whiskey-saturated movies about the lives and times of Guy Clark, Ray Wylie Hubbard, Robert Earl Keen and of course the great Townes Van Zandt.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07blazepix/07blazepix-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07blazepix/07blazepix-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 289}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07blazepix/07blazepix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 493, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07blazepix/07blazepix-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 895, 'width': 1860, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07blazepix/07blazepix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07blazepix/07blazepix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/arts/07blazepix/07blazepix-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Ethan Hawke’s ‘Blaze’ Revisits a Country-Music Legend', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headl