nization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b6d33a2-1333-508c-b8b9-7c5ce4ba1866', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b6d33a2-1333-508c-b8b9-7c5ce4ba1866'}, {'abstract': 'The convoluted and baldly political history of “home rule,” the legal quirk that allows the state to make decisions for New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/07/nyregion/albany-to-city-drop-dead.html', 'snippet': 'The convoluted and baldly political history of “home rule,” the legal quirk that allows the state to make decisions for New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regardless of where you stand on banning plastic bags, regulating speeding cars near schools, or how to fix the subways, most New York City residents are probably asking the same question: Why are those decisions being made in Albany by the governor and the state Legislature instead of in City Hall by the mayor and the City Council?', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09HOMERULE/merlin_143274948_77aaa5af-e038-4082-9bb8-28d38d9ac0c5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 563, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09HOMERULE/merlin_143274948_77aaa5af-e038-4082-9bb8-28d38d9ac0c5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 563}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09HOMERULE/merlin_143274948_77aaa5af-e038-4082-9bb8-28d38d9ac0c5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 961, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09HOMERULE/merlin_143274948_77aaa5af-e038-4082-9bb8-28d38d9ac0c5-superJumbo.jpg', '