article/56c34cd3-5364-56d4-8adb-138d8ac4105b'}, {'abstract': 'Championships won’t get locked up for another three months, but Week 2 is college football’s nuttiest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/07/sports/college-football-week-2-upsets.html', 'snippet': 'Championships won’t get locked up for another three months, but Week 2 is college football’s nuttiest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An eventual national champion sustains its only loss of the year. A Mid-American Conference team goes on the road and scores twice as many points as its Big Ten opponent. A celebrated former player who is now the athletic director materializes on the sideline and argues with the referees. A lower-tier team accomplishes one of the biggest upsets in history.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/08/sports/08week2/08week2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/08/sports/08week2/08week2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/08/sports/08week2/08week2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/08/sports/08week2/08week2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/08/sports/08week2/08week2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/08/sports/08week2/08week2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/08/sports/08week2/08week2-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'College Football’s Craziest Weekend Arrives', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beware Week 2, When Distraction and Hubris Bring Upsets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-07T09:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Tracy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tracy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/030da44a-cd42-593b-b7c6-cd7f9d50023d', 'word_count': 1177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/030da44a-cd42-593b-b7c6-cd7f9d50023d'}, {'abstract': 'Besides making videos for the Love Vote, a new nonprofit, the high school senior likes to stroll and eat dumplings in Chinatown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/07/nyregion/how-aicha-cherif-student-activist-spends-her-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'Besides making videos for the Love Vote, a new nonprofit, the high school senior likes to stroll and eat dumplings in Chinatown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aicha Cherif, 17, just started her senior year at School of the Future in Manhattan. But her responsibilities don’t stop with homework; she is also the outreach director for the Love Vote, which provides a platform for people who can’t vote to encourage those that can to do so. It is understandable why the teenager was drawn to the nonprofit: Ms. Cherif herself will not be eligible to vote when she turns 18 next May. When she was a baby, her family immigrated to the United States from Guinea. Now a permanent resident, Ms. Cherif has recruited 100 people to vote so far. She lives with her grandparents, Aissatou Toure and Zakaria Fofana, on the Lower East Side of Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09ROUTINE01/09ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09ROUTINE01/09ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09ROUTINE01/09ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09ROUTINE01/09ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09ROUTINE01/09ROUTINE01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09ROUTINE01/09ROUTINE01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/nyregion/09ROUTINE01/09ROUTINE01-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Aicha Cherif, Student Activist, Spends Her Sundays', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Activism Starts Early and Stays Up Late', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'School of the Future', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chinatown (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'The Love Vote', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aicha Cherif', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-07T09:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tammy La Gorce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tammy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Gorce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21024945-1820-5d5c-92b5-a0940883b93b', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21024945-1820-5d5c-92b5-a0940883b93b'}, {'abstract': 'At a retrospective at the Whitney Museum, the life and work of the artist and AIDS activist are a model for making art out of political anger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/07/magazine/the-rage-and-tenderness-of-david-wojnarowiczs-art.html', 'snippet': 'At a retrospective at the Whitney Museum, the life and work of the artist and AIDS activist are a model for making art out of political anger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you know one work by David Wojnarowicz, it is probably “One Day This Kid,” a black-and-white self-portrait of the artist as a prepubescent, surrounded by text. This kid is wearing suspenders and a gee-whiz face, all forehead and chin and two buck teeth. His ears stick out like satellite dishes. It’s the early ’60s, and Wojnarowicz looks as if he walked into the Sears photo studio directly from the set of “Leave it to Beaver.” Then you read the words.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/magazine/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7-articleLarge.png', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/06/magazine/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 601}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/magazine/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1022, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/magazine/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7-superJumbo.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2043, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/magazine/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/06/magazine/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/magazine/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7/mag-wojnarowicz-slide-Z3V7-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rage and Tenderness of David Wojnarowicz’s Art', 'kicker': 'Fea