e', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Victor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Victor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/6000e2a9-9ea9-5a18-af94-cfdc80ebdeba', 'word_count': 1377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6000e2a9-9ea9-5a18-af94-cfdc80ebdeba'}, {'abstract': 'They’re not restraining Trump. They’re making him more powerful. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/07/opinion/columnists/kavanaugh-trump-kamala-harris-anonymous.html', 'snippet': 'They’re not restraining Trump. They’re making him more powerful. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday, the second day of Brett Kavanaugh’s Supreme Court confirmation hearing, Senator Kamala Harris, Democrat of California, asked him a straightforward question about Robert Mueller, the special counsel. “Have you discussed Mueller or his investigation with anyone at Kasowitz Benson and Torres, the law firm founded by Marc Kasowitz, President Trump’s personal lawyer?” Harris asked. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07goldbergWeb/07goldbergWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07goldbergWeb/07goldbergWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07goldbergWeb/07goldbergWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07goldbergWeb/07goldbergWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07goldbergWeb/07goldbergWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07goldbergWeb/07goldbergWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07goldbergWeb/07goldbergWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Corrupt Bargain of the Adults in the Room', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kavanaugh, Brett M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-07T09:45:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Columnists', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fb3fc1a-735e-5801-9492-cdc4ccbf0466', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fb3fc1a-735e-5801-9492-cdc4ccbf0466'}, {'abstract': 'Direct talks between America and the insurgents would be the best way to start diplomacy that might end the war in Afghanistan. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/07/opinion/afghanistan-taliban-trump-talks.html', 'snippet': 'Direct talks between America and the insurgents would be the best way to start diplomacy that might end the war in Afghanistan. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'In July, The Times reported that the Trump administration directed the State Department to open direct talks with the Afghan Taliban, to see whether formal talks between the Afghan government and the Taliban are possible. Taliban officials soon claimed to have met with American diplomats, an assertion that American officials have not publicly commented on. This week, Secretary of State Mike Pompeo announced while on his way to Pakistan that Zalmay Khalilzad, a former ambassador to Afghanistan, would become an adviser on achieving reconciliation there. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07Lute-McDoonald/merlin_104980169_dcaf9b42-83b1-4307-9b7d-ced381d8c8a6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07Lute-McDoonald/merlin_104980169_dcaf9b42-83b1-4307-9b7d-ced381d8c8a6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07Lute-McDoonald/merlin_104980169_dcaf9b42-83b1-4307-9b7d-ced381d8c8a6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07Lute-McDoonald/merlin_104980169_dcaf9b42-83b1-4307-9b7d-ced381d8c8a6-superJumbo