s around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Urdu novel published in 1869 by Nazir Ahmad, a writer in Delhi, portrays two young Muslim girls at their geography lesson. As they identify various countries on a map, the girls come across the Arabian Peninsula. Their teacher describes it as an empty space infested by marauding Bedouin, one whose only significance lay in its historical role as the site of Islam’s birth. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07devji/07devji-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07devji/07devji-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07devji/07devji-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07devji/07devji-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1485, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07devji/07devji-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07devji/07devji-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/opinion/07devji/07devji-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Saudi Arabia Cease to Be the Center of Islam?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilgrimages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mecca (Saudi Arabia)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-07T10:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Faisal Devji', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Faisal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Devji', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8f1ca81-7ed6-56c1-a0c8-1c9408167a4c', 'word_count': 1199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8f1ca81-7ed6-56c1-a0c8-1c9408167a4c'}, {'abstract': 'In “Proving Up,” Missy Mazzoli tries to meet the high expectations set by her seething adaptation of the film “Breaking the Waves.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/07/arts/music/missy-mazzoli-proving-up-opera.html', 'snippet': 'In “Proving Up,” Missy Mazzoli tries to meet the high expectations set by her seething adaptation of the film “Breaking the Waves.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the New York premiere of “Proving Up,” at the Miller Theater on Sept. 26 and 28, the composer Missy Mazzoli has that contemporary musical miracle: a hotly anticipated third opera, a voice intriguing enough to seek out again and again.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/arts/09MISSYCOMPOSER4web/merlin_143013168_0e6415a2-383f-450