ri': 'nyt://article/5b8cb542-1642-5f55-b16d-9dce1213c3da'}, {'abstract': 'A by-no-means exhaustive list of the things our editors (and a few contributors) find interesting this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/07/t-magazine/prada-nylon-bag-matches-fashion-store-editors-picks.html', 'snippet': 'A by-no-means exhaustive list of the things our editors (and a few contributors) find interesting this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first luxury good I ever coveted, which my grandmother bought for me, was a black nylon Prada bag. It was a cross-body that I wore with everything for years, and it was the start of my love affair with Prada. It led to my next obsession: Prada’s classic Linea Rossa collection of high-tech streamlined pieces made from sportswear nylon, which debuted in 1997 and soon became a hallmark of the brand. Now, Prada is relaunching the collection for a new generation of fans. Last February, Miuccia Prada closed her fall 2018 show with a series of nylon pullover jackets and bucket hats in an array of acidic neon hues, all bearing the Linea Rossa logo, a sleek red stripe. The new collection, which launches this weekend, retains the minimalist ’90s sensibility of the original line but features an updated fabric. Anoraks, padded jackets, quilted pants and bucket hats (there are also angular wraparound sunglasses) all come in a more technical, waterproof and windproof nylon, in a rainbow of new colors including highlighter pink, safety orange and bright mint green. Available at Prada stores worldwide, select boutiques and prada.com — MALINA JOSEPH GILCHRIST', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/21/t-magazine/fashion/Tel-slide-RZE0/Tel-slide-RZE0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/21/t-magazine/fashion/Tel-slide-RZE0/Tel-slide-RZ