headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-09-07T22:47:02+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/52771456-afae-56cd-b100-d8ad04c43950', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/52771456-afae-56cd-b100-d8ad04c43950'}, {'abstract': 'Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen of the Row and Simon Porte Jacquemus are also among those turning their attention to men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/07/t-magazine/fashion/prabal-gurung-menswear.html', 'snippet': 'Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen of the Row and Simon Porte Jacquemus are also among those turning their attention to men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ladies first. Men’s wear to follow. A number of fashion designers who have made a name for themselves for their women’s wear lines are turning their attention to men. On Sunday evening, at Spring Studios, during New York Fashion Week’s women’s ready-to-wear collections, the designer Prabal Gurung, will debut a men’s wear line alongside his women’s wear, which he first launched in 2009. This October, Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen’s the Row will offer its first men’s wear collection directly through retailers. Speculation surrounds Hedi Slimane, who will present his first men’s and women’s collections at Paris Fashion Week for Céline since taking over the house — which until now only released clothing for women. And earlier this summer, the French designer Simon Porte Jacquemus, of Jacquemus, showed his first men’s wear collection in Calanque de Sormiou, a seaside cove located on the outskirts of Marseille. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/07/t-magazine/fashion/women-designers-slide-B175/women-designers-slid