'nyt://article/16929d7a-df5d-546f-816f-cfe3e36396af', 'word_count': 39, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16929d7a-df5d-546f-816f-cfe3e36396af'}, {'abstract': 'President Bashar al-Assad’s forces are about to attack Idlib, the last rebel-held province in Syria. Fear of mass slaughter is increasing. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/08/opinion/sunday/syria-idlib-assad.html', 'snippet': 'President Bashar al-Assad’s forces are about to attack Idlib, the last rebel-held province in Syria. Fear of mass slaughter is increasing. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first thing that struck me when I saw Idlib, the rebel-held province in northwestern Syria, in April last year was how green the country was. Olive and cherry trees lined the pockmarked roads leading from the Turkish border down to the province’s towns. Smoke rose in the distance in the aftermath of an airstrike or an exploding shell, and the buildings in most towns were scarred by blows from the sky. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/opinion/sunday/09shaheen1/merlin_143334768_7ad799c2-075c-420e-9457-5f92edb0d813-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/09/opinion/sunday/09shaheen1/merlin_143334768_7ad799c2-075c-420e-9457-5f92edb0d813-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/opinion/sunday/09shaheen1/merlin_143334768_7ad799c2-075c-420e-9457-5f92edb0d813-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/09/opinion/sunday/09shaheen1/merlin_143334768_7ad799c2-075c-420e-9457-5f92edb0d813