 transformed by acid house music and the drug Ecstasy — with, surprisingly, a little help from a group of flier designers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — In early 1988, Danny Rampling, a D.J., asked George Georgiou to design a flier for his club night Shoom in a south London fitness center.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/arts/11summeroflove-top-image/summeroflove-top-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/11/arts/11summeroflove-top-image/summeroflove-top-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 656}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/arts/11summeroflove-top-image/summeroflove-top-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 936, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/arts/11summeroflove-top-image/summeroflove-top-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1872, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/arts/11summeroflove-top-image/summeroflove-top-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/11/arts/11summeroflove-top-image/summeroflove-top-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/arts/11summeroflove-top-image/summeroflove-top-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In 1988, Acid House Swept Britain. These Fliers Tell the Story. ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Graphic Art Tells Story Of Acid House Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ecstasy (Drug)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-10T07:54:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Marshall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marshall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b6e1638-3266-53bc-a64e-a1587c9778f2', 'word_count': 1059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b6e1638-3266-53bc-a64e-a1587c9778f2'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Parks realized the power of empathy to help people understand poverty. In this 1961 photo essay, he took readers inside the lives of a Brazilian boy, Flavio da Silva, and his family, who lived in a favela in the hills outside Rio de Janeiro.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/10/lens/gordon-parks-on-poverty-the-most-savage-of-human-afflictions.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Parks realized the power of empathy to help people understand poverty. In this 1961 photo essay, he took readers inside the lives of a Brazilian boy, Flavio da Silva, and his family, who lived in a favela in the hills outside Rio de Janeiro.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Empathy for the poor may not come easily to people who never experienced poverty. They may blame the victims and insist their predicament can be overcome through determination and hard work. But they may not realize that extreme poverty can be psychologically and physically incapacitating — a perpetual cycle of bad diets, health care and education exacerbated by the shaming and self-fulfilling prophecies that define it in the public imagination.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/10/lens/10flavio13-alpha/10flavio13-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 606, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/10/lens/10flavio13-alpha/10flavio13-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 606}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/10/lens/10flavio13-alpha/10flavio13-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1015, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/10/lens/10flavio13-alpha/10flavio13-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1514, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/10/lens/10flavio13-alpha/10flavio13-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/10/lens/10flavio13-alpha/10flavio13-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/10/lens/10flavio13-alpha/10flavio13-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gordon Parks on Poverty, the ‘Most Savage of Human Afflictions’', 'kicker': 'RACE STORIES', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': N