er': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5204700-9276-5eb9-a2dc-4b23be7625b5', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5204700-9276-5eb9-a2dc-4b23be7625b5'}, {'abstract': 'With two more high-profile plays opening in New York this season — and a huge movie deal in the works — Theresa Rebeck’s time may have come.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/10/theater/theresa-rebeck-bernhardt-hamlet-smash.html', 'snippet': 'With two more high-profile plays opening in New York this season — and a huge movie deal in the works — Theresa Rebeck’s time may have come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sarah Bernhardt ran her own theater. Correction: She owned her own theater, which she also ran. It had a dressing room that was actually five rooms, with a marble fireplace. Writers like Victor Hugo and Edmond Rostand lined up to create new works for her. And if Bernhardt preferred to perform a classic, she could put on tights and play Hamlet for an audience of 1,700.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '37', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/arts/16rebeck11/merlin_142493388_32c99276-95c3-42bc-a85c-bbce18c50324-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/16/arts/16rebeck11/merlin_142493388_32c99276-95c3-42bc-a85c-bbce18c50324-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/arts/16rebeck11/merlin_142493388_32c99276-95c3-42bc-a85c-bbce18c50324-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/0