type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17495bc8-4ac8-5c03-aa5b-00f45179c51d', 'word_count': 1810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17495bc8-4ac8-5c03-aa5b-00f45179c51d'}, {'abstract': 'Lesandro Guzman-Feliz, known as Junior, did not belong to a gang, but some of his friends did. In the end, it didn’t matter. Our investigation may help answer why he was targeted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/10/nyregion/lesandro-guzman-feliz-bronx-stabbing-video.html', 'snippet': 'Lesandro Guzman-Feliz, known as Junior, did not belong to a gang, but some of his friends did. In the end, it didn’t matter. Our investigation may help answer why he was targeted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The vicious murder of a 15-year-old boy at the hands of men wielding knives and machetes outside of a Bronx bodega shook New Yorkers this summer like few other crimes in recent memory. Crude footage showing the killing of Lesandro Guzman-Feliz, who was called Junior, went viral.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How a 15-Year-Old Ended Up Stabbed to Death Outside a Bronx Bodega', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gangs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guzman-Feliz, Lesandro', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-10T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Luis Ferré-Sadurní and Barbara Marcolini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Luis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ferré-Sadurní', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marcolini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dfc4b6c-c80e-51c8-8df1-9dfb4b97f588', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dfc4b6c-c80e-51c8-8df1-9dfb4b97f588'}, {'abstract': 'Tai chi moves can be easily learned and executed by people of all ages and states of health, even elderly people in wheelchairs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/10/well/move/using-tai-chi-to-build-strength.html', 'snippet': 'Tai chi moves can be easily learned and executed by people of all ages and states of health, even elderly people in wheelchairs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watching a group of people doing tai chi, an exercise often called “meditation in motion,” it may be hard to imagine that its slow, gentle, choreographed movements could actually make people stronger. Not only stronger mentally but stronger physically and healthier as well. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/science/11BRODYPARTIALSELVES/merlin_143261946_7f1abdc4-6414-4a71-af29-544c1316344e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/16/science/11BRODYPARTIALSELVES/merlin_143261946_7f1abdc4-6414-4a71-af29-544c1316344e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/science/11BRODYPARTIALSELVES/merlin_143261946_7f1abdc4-6414-4a71-af29-544c1316344e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/science/11BRODYPARTIALSELVES/m