persons', 'value': 'Peterman, Nathan (1994- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-10T14:23:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Mather', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mather', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16095eb4-9a63-581a-95dc-25d3a18498ee', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16095eb4-9a63-581a-95dc-25d3a18498ee'}, {'abstract': 'Melissa Clark has a new recipe for bay leaf chicken, and David Tanis one for angel hair pasta with peppers and tomatoes. Make those soon, if not tonight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/10/dining/what-to-cook-right-now-cooking.html', 'snippet': 'Melissa Clark has a new recipe for bay leaf chicken, and David Tanis one for angel hair pasta with peppers and tomatoes. Make those soon, if not tonight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. I was thinking of that Raymond Carver short story, “Chef’s House,” where this guy Wes stays sober in a borrowed house all summer, having left his girlfriend and having convinced his wife, Edna, to leave her boyfriend to live again with him. The house is on the beach, north of Eureka, in California. The couple drinks fruit juice every day and goes to the movies on Tuesdays, and eventually Edna puts her wedding ring back on, and everything’s great. Then Chef, who owns the place, throws them a curveball. They have to leave the house. Wes doesn’t like it much. He gets a little squirrelly, doesn’t talk. “Wes got up and pulled the drapes, and the ocean was gone — just like that,” is how Carver puts it at the end.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/dining/12apperex1-copy/12apperex1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/12/dining/12apperex1-copy/12apperex1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/dining/12apperex1-copy/12apperex1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/dining/12apperex1-copy/12apperex1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/dining/12apperex1-copy/12apperex1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/12/dining/12apperex1-copy/12apperex1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/dining/12apperex1-copy/12apperex1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Cook Right Now', 'kicker': 'What to Cook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-10T14:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de61251f-f565-5289-ba90-90e7c8ca621b', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de61251f-f565-5289-ba90-90e7c8ca621b'}, {'abstract': 'At Bar Moxy in Midtown Manhattan, a vending machine serves ice cream.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/10/dining/ice-cream-vending-machine-moxy.html', 'snippet': 'At Bar Moxy in Midtown Manhattan, a vending machine serves ice cream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a sweet pick-me-up almost any time, there’s soft-serve on demand at Bar Moxy in the Moxy Times Square hotel. A soft-serve vending machine is stationed at the entrance to the bar, though you need not patronize the bar, or even the hotel for that matter, to use it. Cash, credit or Apple Pay are accepted for a swirl of dairy-free dark chocolate, Mike’s Hot Honey vanilla or a twist of both in a cup that appears in a moment or two at a lighted door; a spoon emerges from a slot. Bits of honeycomb, black crumble cookie, rainbow sprinkles or Greek yogurt chips are the optional toppings. It’s a collaboration with the artist Curtis Kulig and bears his signature Love Me logo.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/dining/12burner6/12burner6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/12/dining/12burner6/12burner6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/dining/12burner6/12burner6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/dining/12burner6/12burner6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1395,