ype_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96b68b7f-f504-51c2-aed3-61463768f465', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96b68b7f-f504-51c2-aed3-61463768f465'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. DeSantis, a three-term congressman, is locked in an intense battle for Florida governor against Andrew Gillum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/10/us/florida-ron-desantis-governor.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. DeSantis, a three-term congressman, is locked in an intense battle for Florida governor against Andrew Gillum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — Standing between the American and Cuban flags and surrounded by faded black-and-white photos of anti-Communist combatants, Ron DeSantis did on Monday what many a Florida politician has done before: pay homage to the Cuban exiles who have remained faithful to the Republican Party for generations, the rare Latinos who vote reliably conservative.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/us/11desantis_xp/merlin_143572131_7bf21396-991e-4ec0-a80b-1645709e0279-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/11/us/11desantis_xp/merlin_143572131_7bf21396-991e-4ec0-a80b-1645709e0279-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/us/11desantis_xp/merlin_143572131_7bf21396-991e-4ec0-a80b-1645709e0279-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/us/11desantis_xp/merlin_143572131_7bf21396-991e-4ec0-a80b-1645709e0279-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/us/11desantis_xp/11desantis_xp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/11/us/11desantis_xp/11desantis_xp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/us/11desantis_xp/11desantis_xp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Florida, DeSantis Hopes to Woo Latinos — Not Just Cubans — by Denouncing ‘Socialism’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans Push to Woo Latinos by Denouncing ‘Socialism’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeSantis, Ron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cuban-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillum, Andrew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2018)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nelson, Bill (1942- )', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-10T16:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Mazzei', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzei', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6693ba5-1822-54eb-b7df-dc2ece747c56', 'word_count': 1385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6693ba5-1822-54eb-b7df-dc2ece747c56'}, {'abstract': 'Bruce Goff’s midcentury houses across the Midwest are symbols of both a heartland-born eccentricity and a distinct Modernism. So why has he been forgotten?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/10/t-magazine/bruce-goff-architecture-midwest.html', 'snippet': 'Bruce Goff’s midcentury houses across the Midwest are symbols of both a heartland-born eccentricity and a distinct Modernism. So why has he been forgotten?', 'lead_paragraph': 'AURORA, ILL., 45 miles west of Chicago, lies deep in suburbia: It’s the fictional setting of “Wayne’s World” and the real-life setting of my adolescent weekends at the mall. Behind a commercial strip lined with big-box stores, among the split-levels and center-hall colonials, in the kind of neighborhood where kids run through sprinklers on summer weekends, crouches a massive mushroom-cap dome, 48 feet in diameter. Formed by bright red Quonset hut ribs and flanked by two smaller partial domes, the structure — whose windowless front is done in inky coal masonry studded with rough-hewn chunks of aquamarine glass — looks like a spaceship that’s pulled up its jet bridge. From the back, where its red exoskeleton is exposed, it resembles a birdcage. This is the Ford House, designed in 1947 by Bruce Goff, a prolific and startlingly original midcentury architect who remains, outside of design circles, largely unknown.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/10/t-magazine/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/10/t-magazine/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/10/t-magazine/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/10/t-magazine/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/10/t-magazine/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/10/t-magazine/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/10/t-magazine/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK/10tmag-goff-slide-52CK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Man Who Made Wildly Imaginative, Gloriously Disobedient Buildings', 'kicker': 'Rediscovery', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles County Museum of Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Oklahoma', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Frank Lloyd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Twain, Mark', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huxtable, Ada Louise', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Aurora (Ill)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-10T16:42:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Fortini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fortini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a78c41e5-0237-5244-a2fd-6e229ddc594d', 'word_count': 2056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a78c41e5-0237-5244-a2fd-6e229ddc594d'}, {'abstract': 'In this stage memoir, Chesney Show struggles to balance a powerful personal story with historical heft.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/10/theater/review-unwritten-law-chesney-show.html', 'snippet': 'In this stage memoir, Chesney Show struggles to balance a powerful personal story with historical heft.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I am, and we are, the new law that has not been written,” Chesney Snow proclaims at the conclusion of his autobiographical mixed-media stage show, “The Unwritten Law,” at Dixon Place. It’s a broad, vague political declaration, delivered at the end of a monologue that covers, in a scant few minutes, the black experience in America from slavery to mass incarceration, name-dropping Talib Kweli and Martin Luther King Jr. along the way.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/theater/11unwrittenlaw/merlin_1430