ar that the United States would exit the Paris climate deal, a broad group of governors, mayors and business executives declared that they would uphold the agreement anyway and continue tackling global warming on their own.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/science/12cli-states-01/merlin_143557794_8b23b983-6677-407e-8a1b-aaf1d8e26d01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/12/science/12cli-states-01/merlin_143557794_8b23b983-6677-407e-8a1b-aaf1d8e26d01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/science/12cli-states-01/merlin_143557794_8b23b983-6677-407e-8a1b-aaf1d8e26d01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/science/12cli-states-01/merlin_143557794_8b23b983-6677-407e-8a1b-aaf1d8e26d01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1534, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/science/12cli-states-01/12cli-states-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/12/science/12cli-states-01/12cli-states-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/science/12cli-states-01/12cli-states-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'They Defied Trump on Climate Change. Now, It’s Their Moment of Truth. ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Local Leaders Defied Trump on Climate Change. Can They Deliver?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Inslee, Jay', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-11T15:38:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Climate', 'section_name': 'Climate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Plumer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Plumer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e1af303-5b55-585f-bb65-0f4fb5e79fb7', 'word_count': 1221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e1af303-5b55-585f-bb65-0f4fb5e79fb7'}, {'abstract': 'The patient has a mutation in the KCNMA1 gene. Can you help us find others who share this abnormality?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/11/magazine/a-diagnosis-update-new-information-on-a-young-girls-rare-genetic-condition.html', 'snippet': 'The patient has a mutation in the KCNMA1 gene. Can you help us find others who share this abnormality?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week I presented the case of the 6-year-old girl in South Dakota who had episodes of transient muscle weakness dozens of times a day, starting around the time she turned 1. The events seemed to be triggered by strong emotions, particularly joy. She had thorough work-ups as neurologists, first in South Dakota, then at the Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minn., tried to figure out the cause of these odd spells. Just before she turned 4, Kamiyah was accepted into the National Institutes of Health’s Undiagnosed Diseases Network — truly the diagnosticians of last resort. She spent a week in Bethesda, Md., getting test after test, as doctors there searched for disorders that could cause the symptoms she was experiencing. All that testing finally produced an answer: She had a genetic abnormality causing these attacks of muscular weakness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/magazine/06diagnosis-kamiyah-image/06diagnosis-kamiyah-image-articleLarge.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/06/magazine/06diagnosis-kamiyah-image/06diagnosis-kamiyah-image-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/magazine/06diagnosis-kamiyah-image/06diagnosis-kamiyah-image-jumbo.png', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/magazine/06diagnosis-kamiyah-image/06diagnosis-kamiyah-image-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0