, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4afcc526-f4ba-52dd-b80c-6928bb742ecc', 'word_count': 2510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4afcc526-f4ba-52dd-b80c-6928bb742ecc'}, {'abstract': 'Marie Foulston is the curator of video games at the Victoria and Albert Museum in London. Her first exhibition shows how games can break new ground.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/11/arts/design/video-games-curator-victoria-albert-museum.html', 'snippet': 'Marie Foulston is the curator of video games at the Victoria and Albert Museum in London. Her first exhibition shows how games can break new ground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Last week, Marie Foulston stood in the Victoria and Albert Museum trying to explain what was so groundbreaking about a host of recent video games. At the same time, she was trying to play one, controlling a horse onscreen that was, absurdly, driving a taxi cab.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/arts/12videogames1/merlin_143556579_0509d7a2-c58f-49c4-a99f-70d98af29061-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/12/arts/12videogames1/merlin_143556579_0509d7a2-c58f-49c4-a99f-70d98af29061-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/arts/12videogames1/merlin_143556579_0509d7a2-c58f-49c4-a99f-70d98af29061-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/arts/12videogames1/merlin_143556579_0509d7a2-c58f-49c4-a99f-70d98af29061-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'su