se staff members are nonwhite, a new study shows — a far smaller figure than in the United States as a whole or among House lawmakers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/11/us/politics/diversity-congress-house-republicans-democrats.html', 'snippet': 'Just 14 percent of top House staff members are nonwhite, a new study shows — a far smaller figure than in the United States as a whole or among House lawmakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — House aides write federal policy and multitrillion-dollar budgets, oversee the administration of government and shape the public’s view of Congress, but the top staff members of the House of Representatives are far less racially diverse than the country itself — or even the lawmakers who employ them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/us/politics/12dc-house/12dc-house-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/12/us/politics/12dc-house/12dc-house-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/us/politics/12dc-house/12dc-house-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/us/politics/12dc-house/12dc-house-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/us/politics/12dc-house/12dc-house-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/12/us/politics/12dc-house/12dc-house-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/us/politics/12dc-house/12dc-house-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In an Increasingly Diverse House, Aides Remain Remarkably White', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Hallways of Congress, a Lot of White Faces', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-11T19:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Fandos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fandos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0c71e90-dfd9-548e-abd0-3ac2d0071ebd', 'word_count': 1163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0c71e90-dfd9-548e-abd0-3ac2d0071ebd'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Jorge Pardo designed the interiors of L’Arlatan, which opens next month in Arles, France.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/11/t-magazine/design/jose-pardo-arlatan-hotel-arles-france.html', 'snippet': 'The artist Jorge Pardo designed the interiors of L’Arlatan, which opens next month in Arles, France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The artist Jorge Pardo makes work that not only lives outside the confines of the traditional white cube but also interrogates notions of space and setting and our place within them. One of his best-known pieces dates to 1998, when, for a show with the Museum of Contemporary Art, Los Angeles, he designed a single-story house in the city’s Cypress Park neighborhood and filled it with objects of his own making. Once the exhibition closed, Pardo moved in. “I’m essentially appropriating architecture,” says Pardo, who now lives in Mérida, Mexico, in another structure that could be considered both art piece and functional living space — a “birdcage in the jungle” complete with a hand-painted mural and ovoid pendant lights.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '53', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/t-magazine/11tmag-pardo-slide-0I29/11tmag-pardo-slide-0I29-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 880, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/11/t-magazine/11tmag-pardo-slide-0I29/11tmag-pardo-slide-0I29-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 880}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/t-magazine/11tmag-pardo-slide-0I29/11tmag-pardo-slide-0I29-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 698, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/11/t-magazine/11tmag-pardo-slide-0I29/11tmag-pardo-slide-0I29-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1278, 'width': 871, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legac