tle': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b678956-35b8-50d2-a791-7c39a5426d5d', 'word_count': 1399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b678956-35b8-50d2-a791-7c39a5426d5d'}, {'abstract': 'The night before her film debut, the actress sat on her bed in a Valentino gown and asked herself, “Girl, what is your life right now?”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/11/movies/kiki-layne-if-beale-street-could-talk.html', 'snippet': 'The night before her film debut, the actress sat on her bed in a Valentino gown and asked herself, “Girl, what is your life right now?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The night before “If Beale Street Could Talk” had its premiere at the Toronto International Film Festival, the movie’s leading lady, KiKi Layne, found herself sleepless in couture. She had just left a party where everyone knew her director, Barry Jenkins, whose last film was the best-picture winner “Moonlight.” But the 26-year-old Ms. Layne, who makes her film debut in “Beale Street,” was still a mystery to people. And the next day, she would no longer be.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/arts/13kiki-layne/merlin_143523702_cfe43806-3d62-4209-befb-db86f2ce9d8b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 893, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/13/arts/13kiki-layne/merlin_143523702_cfe43806-3d62-4209-befb-db86f2ce9d8b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 893}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/arts/13kiki-layne/merlin_143523702_cfe43806-3d62-4209-befb-db86f2ce9d8b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': '