-war-i.html', 'snippet': 'Nearly a quarter of the men sent to fight in Europe in 1918 were foreign-born.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A hundred years ago this week, on a bend of the Meuse River in northern France, Gen. John Pershing launched the final major Allied offensive against Germany, an assault that would bring an end to World War I two months later. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/opinion/12wawro/12wawro-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/12/opinion/12wawro/12wawro-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/opinion/12wawro/12wawro-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/opinion/12wawro/12wawro-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/opinion/12wawro/12wawro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/12/opinion/12wawro/12wawro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/opinion/12wawro/12wawro-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How ‘Hyphenated Americans’ Won World War I', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pershing, John Joseph', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-12T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoffrey Wawro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wawro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/99a9baa0-1935-5b54-bd65-f8759e33cf70', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99a9baa0-1935-5b54-bd65-f8759e33cf70'}, {'abstract': 'When we firefighters step into a life-threatening situation, we need to work as a team. Hate and discrimination within our ranks make that impossible. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/12/opinion/the-racism-inside-fire-departments.html', 'snippet': 'When we firefighters step into a life-threatening situation, we need to work as a team. Hate and discrimination within our ranks make that impossible. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine how you would feel if you showed up at work and found a noose waiting for you. It happened just last year to a young black firefighter in Miami. In our profession, that garish expression of racism was unfortunately not an anomaly. In the aftermath of California’s summer wildfires and the well-deserved praise of the heroism of the people who risked their lives to extinguish them, it’s also important to confront the bigotry that puts individual firefighters and the people we serve at risk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'ran