uette recalls a pill or a bullet. As a floral arrangement, it redefines the term: The flower appears isolated, dwarfed by its container, perhaps near death. Yet herein lies its power, in the tension between soft and hard, fleeting and fixed, the fragility of natural beauty and the steady gleam of the man-made. It’s a radically minimalist composition, revealing less the hand of its designer, Louis-Géraud Castor of Castor-Fleuriste in Paris, and more his mind.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '176', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-disruptors/12tmag-disruptors-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-disruptors/12tmag-disruptors-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-disruptors/12tmag-disruptors-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-disruptors/12tmag-disruptors-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1451, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-disruptors/12tmag-disruptors-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-disruptors/12tmag-disruptors-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '