ank vault in Paris during World War II. He never saw it again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/12/nyregion/nazi-art-renoir.html', 'snippet': 'The painting belonged to a Jewish art dealer when it was taken from a bank vault in Paris during World War II. He never saw it again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1970s, it changed hands in Johannesburg and London. More recently, it was sold for $180,000 in New York and, for $390,000, in Michigan by a gallery known for selling fine art on cruise ships.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/nyregion/13naziart2/merlin_143639379_479a49ee-5609-4b8e-b75a-9b05429f27b9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/13/nyregion/13naziart2/merlin_143639379_479a49ee-5609-4b8e-b75a-9b05429f27b9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/nyregion/13naziart2/merlin_143639379_479a49ee-5609-4b8e-b75a-9b05429f27b9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/nyregion/13naziart2/merlin_143639379_479a49ee-5609-4b8e-b75a-9b05429f27b9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/nyregion/13naziart2/merlin_143639379_479a49ee-5609-4b8e-b75a-9b05429f27b9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/13/nyregion/13naziart2/merlin_143639379_479a49ee-5609-4b8e-b75a-9b05429f27b9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/nyregion/13naziart2/merlin_143639379_479a49ee-5609-4b8e-b75a-9b05429f27b9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nazis Stole His Renoir. His Granddaughter Finally Got It Back.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stolen by the Nazis, A Renoir Is Returned To a Descendant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arts and Antiquities Looting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Christie's", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Park West Gallery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Jewish Heritage', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Renoir, Pierre Auguste', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-12T15:12:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cd48467-8e1b-5cc6-a8d0-c92518bab7cc', 'word_count': 1437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cd48467-8e1b-5cc6-a8d0-c92518bab7cc'}, {'abstract': 'The website that helped drive demand for streetwear is going IRL with a festival called, you guessed it, Hypefest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/12/style/hypebeast-hypefest.html', 'snippet': 'The website that helped drive demand for streetwear is going IRL with a festival called, you guessed it, Hypefest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you were a young male in the mid-2000s with a vague interest in Japanese denim or limited-colorway Nike Dunks or whatever it was that Pharrell was wearing that month, you may have found your way to Hypebeast, a fashion blog that was among the first to enthusiastically document trends in sneakers and streetwear.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/fashion/13HYPEFEST1/merlin_143609712_bd6aa67e-4d49-4eb1-8a26-1bff20e150bf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/13/fashion/13HYPEFEST1/merlin_143609712_bd6aa67e-4d49-4eb1-8a26-1bff20e150bf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/fashion/13HYPEFEST1/merlin_143609712_bd6aa67e-4d49-4eb1-8a26-1bff20e150bf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/fashion/13HYPEFEST1/merlin_143609712_bd6aa67e-4d49-4eb1-8a26-1bff20e150bf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/fashion/13HYPEFEST1/13HYPEFEST1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/13/fashion/13HYPEFEST1/13HYPEFEST1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidt