vision/bojack-horseman-season-4-recap.html', 'snippet': 'Everyone’s favorite self-destructive horse is back with another season of dark, witty misery. Ready for more? Here’s where we left off.', 'lead_paragraph': '“BoJack Horseman” may be the saddest animated comedy in TV history, and with each new batch of episodes it delves deeper into its unique brand of anthropomorphic misery: dark, witty, culturally literate — but for its loyal fans, thoroughly enjoyable. In Season 4, BoJack (voiced by Will Arnett) was forced to reckon with both his family history and a heap of newfound responsibilities. It didn’t always go so well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/arts/13bojack-walkup-bojack-horseman/13bojack-walkup1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/13/arts/13bojack-walkup-bojack-horseman/13bojack-walkup1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/arts/13bojack-walkup-bojack-horseman/13bojack-walkup1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/arts/13bojack-walkup-bojack-horseman/13bojack-walkup1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1148, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/arts/13bojack-walkup-bojack-horseman/13bojack-walkup1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/13/arts/13bojack-walkup-bojack-horseman/13bojack-walkup