 and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Starr, Kenneth W', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-13T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14513215-1ec3-5971-b1b0-dc454425251a', 'word_count': 1561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14513215-1ec3-5971-b1b0-dc454425251a'}, {'abstract': 'The storm won’t be alone: Tropical cyclones have grown more sluggish since the mid-20th century. Here’s why that’s a bad thing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/13/climate/slow-hurricane-florence.html', 'snippet': 'The storm won’t be alone: Tropical cyclones have grown more sluggish since the mid-20th century. Here’s why that’s a bad thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With wind speeds that have approached 140 miles per hour, Hurricane Florence isn’t exactly slow. But forecasters don’t expect the storm to blow through quickly once it reaches land.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/climate/cli-florence-update/cli-florence-update-articleLarge.png', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/12/climate/cli-florence-update/cli-florence-update-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 366}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/12/climate/cli-florence-update/cli-florence-update-jumbo.png', 'height': 624, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'capti