 have failed. They point out that by one key measure the state now has the highest poverty rate in the nation and they argue that its liberal minimum wage and restrictive housing codes have more than a hundred thousand people homeless, more than a million unemployed and millions more stuck on the bottom rungs of the socioeconomic ladder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/opinion/13edsallSub/merlin_143650395_a111ed61-4960-49f8-8d06-9e8672b6ed68-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/13/opinion/13edsallSub/merlin_143650395_a111ed61-4960-49f8-8d06-9e8672b6ed68-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/opinion/13edsallSub/merlin_143650395_a111ed61-4960-49f8-8d06-9e8672b6ed68-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/opinion/13edsallSub/merlin_143650395_a111ed61-4960-49f8-8d06-9e8672b6ed68-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/opinion/13edsallSub/13edsallSub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/13/opinion/13edsallSub/13edsallSub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/opinion/13edsallSub/13edsallSub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is California a Good Role Model?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Florida, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hendren, Nathaniel B (1982- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pastor, Manuel (1956- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-13T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas B. Edsall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/19270fcb-a917-541d-9a66-a8bb131d8de3', 'word_count': 2483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19270fcb-a917-541d-9a66-a8bb131d8de3'}, {'abstract': 'What will the court look like when neither side of the ideological divide has to walk on eggs to win the favor of the justice in the middle? ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/13/opinion/editorials/kavanaugh-supreme-court-divide.html', 'snippet': 'What will the court look like when neither side of the ideological divide has to walk on eggs to win the favor of the justice in the middle? ', 'lead_paragraph': 'So it’s all over but the voting. I’m writing this column on the assumption that Judge Brett Kavanaugh will soon be Justice Kavanaugh, despite the Democrats’ continuing efforts to convert a futile battle over ideology into an ugly one over transparency and ethics. By the first Monday in October or soon thereafter, the Roberts court version 5.0 (accounting for the earlier arrival of Justices Samuel Alito, Sonia Sotomayor, Elena Kagan and Neil Gorsuch since Chief Justice John Roberts took his seat in September 2005) will be underway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/opinion/13Greenhouse2/merlin_143277369_26fc8fcb-5f2a-48ec-bd5b-08009d18fdcb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/13/opinion/13Greenhouse2/merlin_143277369_26fc8fcb-5f2a-48ec-bd5b-08009d18fdcb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/opinion/13Greenhouse2/merlin_143277369_26fc8fcb-5f2a-48ec-bd5b-08009d18fdcb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/opinion/13Greenhouse2/merlin_143277369_26fc8fcb-5f2a-48ec-bd5b-08009d18fdcb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1374, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/opinion/13Greenhouse2/merlin_143277369_26fc8fcb-5f2a-48ec-bd5b-08009d18fdcb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/13/opinion/13Greenhouse2/merlin_143277369_26fc8fcb-5f2a-48ec-bd5b-08009d18fdcb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, '