': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/89e5713e-5cfd-5236-9869-f374ad8684e6', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89e5713e-5cfd-5236-9869-f374ad8684e6'}, {'abstract': 'The director RaMell Ross has created a movie that is both a narrative of real lives and an inquiry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/13/movies/hale-county-this-morning-this-evening-review-ramell-ross.html', 'snippet': 'The director RaMell Ross has created a movie that is both a narrative of real lives and an inquiry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Russian director Andrei Tarkovsky famously defined the work of a filmmaker as “sculpting in time.” In his book of that title, Tarkovsky elaborated that the filmmaker, starting with “an enormous, solid cluster of living facts,” ought to discard what is not needed and keep only what is “integral to the cinematic image.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/arts/14HALECOUNTY-1/merlin_143417850_2b459dae-9689-4814-a32c-1e0d5efedbf9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/14/arts/14HALECOUNTY-1/merlin_143417850_2b459dae-9689-4814-a32c-1e0d5efedbf9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/arts/14HALECOUNTY-1/merlin_143417850_2b459dae-9689-4814-a32c-1e0d5efedbf9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/arts/14HALECOUN