word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a44590fe-e6bb-5456-981b-c8dcc78cb9d3'}, {'abstract': 'A need for medical treatment conflicts with a family’s religious beliefs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/13/movies/the-children-act-review-emma-thompson.html', 'snippet': 'A need for medical treatment conflicts with a family’s religious beliefs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adapted by Ian McEwan from his 2014 novel and smoothly directed by Richard Eyre, “The Children Act” stars Emma Thompson as Fiona Maye, a British judge who must decide whether to require Adam, a 17-year-old with leukemia, to receive a blood transfusion. Adam is a Jehovah’s Witness, and blood transfusion runs counter to the religion’s tenets and his parents’ beliefs — and therefore his own.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/arts/14childrenact/merlin_143452377_e5669f9e-9ba8-4534-862b-55bc18d055f7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/14/arts/14childrenact/merlin_143452377_e5669f9e-9ba8-4534-862b-55bc18d055f7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/arts/14childrenact/merlin_143452377_e5669f9e-9ba8-4534-862b-55bc18d055f7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/arts/14childrenact/merlin_143452377_e5669f9e-9ba8-4534-862b-55bc18d055f7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/