ne, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/08/21/opinion/21cowie/21cowie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1533, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/08/21/opinion/21cowie/21cowie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/08/21/opinion/21cowie/21cowie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/08/21/opinion/21cowie/21cowie-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pieces of a Flag', 'kicker': 'Picture Prompts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-09-13T11:56:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Proulx', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Proulx', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/812f7a04-a23d-5007-9280-bc5cf8da1ba2', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/812f7a04-a23d-5007-9280-bc5cf8da1ba2'}, {'abstract': 'Marc Chagall and Kasimir Malevich, professors at the same art school in revolutionary Russia, face off in a new exhibition at the Jewish Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/13/arts/design/chagall-lissitzky-malevich-russian-avant-garde-jewish-museum.html', 'snippet': 'Marc Chagall and Kasimir Malevich, professors at the same art school in revolutionary Russia, face off in a new exhibition at the Jewish Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Big egos in small studios, high-pressure critiques and lowlife carousing: If you’re looking for creative drama, there’s nowhere quite like art school. Modern art is the product of trained students much more than of solitary geniuses, and whole chapters of art history were written in schools that became, sometimes just for a few years, epicenters of invention. It happened at the Bauhaus and the Kunstakademie Düsseldorf in Germany, at Goldsmiths and the Glasgow School of Art in Britain, at Black Mountain College and CalArts in the United States — and, 100 years ago, in the bright first days after revolution, it happened at a short-lived art school in a provincial outpost of Russia. In its classrooms, far from the lights of Moscow and the raging civil war, professors and students got to work imagining art for the utopia to come.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/arts/14JewishMuseum1/merlin_143360817_5ce8c510-9939-42ba-a2f2-b1868994cd37-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/14/arts/14JewishMuseum1/merlin_143360817_5ce8c510-9939-42ba-a2f2-b1868994cd37-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/arts/14JewishMuseum1/merlin_143360817_5ce8c510-9939-42ba-a2f2-b1868994cd37-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/arts/14JewishMuseum1/merlin_143360817_5ce8c510-9939-42ba-a2f2-b1868994cd37-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1422, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbn