or a dictator there, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — The Spanish Parliament voted on Thursday to exhume the remains of Francisco Franco, the former dictator, from the underground basilica that he had built near Madrid, intensifying a debate over his legacy that continues 43 years after his death.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/world/14Spain1/merlin_142485519_b5e2717e-f779-4319-864b-f94f166ad5ad-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/14/world/14Spain1/merlin_142485519_b5e2717e-f779-4319-864b-f94f166ad5ad-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/world/14Spain1/merlin_142485519_b5e2717e-f779-4319-864b-f94f166ad5ad-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/world/14Spain1/merlin_142485519_b5e2717e-f779-4319-864b-f94f166ad5ad-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/world/14Spain1/14Spain1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/14/world/14Spain1/14Spain1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/world/14Spain1/14Spain1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spain to Exhume Franco From Monument He Had Built', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Franco’s Body to Be Exhumed, as Debate Over Legacy Grows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spanish Civil War (1936-39)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez Perez-Castejon, Pedro (1972- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franco, Francisco', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ciudadanos Party (Spain)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Podemos (Spanish Political Party)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Popular Party (Spain)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Spanish Socialist Workers' Party", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-13T14:13:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c567fee9-dd83-5145-94b6-2e539e0d8a27', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c567fee9-dd83-5145-94b6-2e539e0d8a27'}, {'abstract': 'There are some traditions that are universal. Here, we highlight a single craft — and how it’s being adapted, rethought and remade for the 21st century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/13/t-magazine/sardinian-weaving-woven-textiles.html', 'snippet': 'There are some traditions that are universal. Here, we highlight a single craft — and how it’s being adapted, rethought and remade for the 21st century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN ISABELLA FRONGIA, 61, perhaps the most gifted weaver in Samugheo, the Sardinian town best known for its textiles, was a little girl, she would watch her mother, Susanna, work for hours at her loom. Located in the entry hall, the loom had been built of oak and chestnut by a local carpenter, and its squared edges had long ago gone smooth to the touch. Susanna, who is now 86, would sit before it, raising alternate strings attached to bamboo poles by pressing on the wooden pedals at her feet. She would send a bobbin of weft thread gliding across the horizontal surface of the remaining strings, strung taut in the loom’s belly, before yanking a heavy hinged wood batten with metal teeth toward herself, locking each new row into the others. This simple gesture — passing a weft thread through a base of stable warp threads — is the same for every piece of cloth ever woven. And on this loom, Susanna made everything the family needed, from bedcovers, blankets and towels to the wool textiles laid atop wood chests and the saddlebags slung over the backs of donkeys or men to transport things. Each piece was crafted according to designs and patterns stored in an unwritten repository of techniques and styles, many unique to the island, which over centuries had been passed through the hands of Sardinia’s women.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '180', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/t-magazine/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/13/t-magazine/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/t-magazine/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/t-magazine/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/t-magazine/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/13/t-magazine/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/13/t-magazine/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07/13tmag-weaving-slide-2Y07-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Sardinian Weaving Nearly Became a Lost Art', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weaving', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rural Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawrence, D H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sardinia (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-13T14:15:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'origin