 customers looked up from their veal marsala and clams casino to consider the stylish spectacle.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/nyregion/16FORLINIS2/16FORLINIS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/16/nyregion/16FORLINIS2/16FORLINIS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/nyregion/16FORLINIS2/16FORLINIS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/nyregion/16FORLINIS2/16FORLINIS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/nyregion/16FORLINIS2/16FORLINIS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/16/nyregion/16FORLINIS2/16FORLINIS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/nyregion/16FORLINIS2/16FORLINIS2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Forlini’s Survives the Instagram Horde', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surviving the Instagram Horde', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Forlini's (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Millennial Generation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Italian Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Little Italy (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-14T09:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Vadukul and Amy Lombard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vadukul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lombard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee8dadd6-c232-5f56-93d4-3316b309c4b9', 'word_count': 1839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee8dadd6-c232-5f56-93d4-3316b309c4b9'}, {'abstract': 'The actress and comedian can move up and down the scales of race, age and gender with hilarious ease — a talent that grew from finding her place in a world where no one looked like her.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/14/magazine/maya-rudolph-snl-amazon-forever.html', 'snippet': 'The actress and comedian can move up and down the scales of race, age and gender with hilarious ease — a talent that grew from finding her place in a world where no one looked like her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Supposing that God is real and possessed of a human corporeal form — mankind being created in his image (reportedly) — we might reasonably conjecture that God’s anthropoid body integrates the totality of physical traits expressed in Earth’s human population: the skin tones blended to a light tan; the hair dark and thick; the height neither too tall nor too short — about 5-foot-7, say; every shade of human iris (the iridescent blue of a morpho butterfly, the pale green of lichen clinging to a tree, lots of brown) combining to create eyes that are ... also brown. Considering his propensity for giving life, God would probably be a mother. Considering his appreciation of beauty (e.g., snowflake geometry) and busy schedule (e.g., Genesis), he would probably clothe himself in breezily tasteful garments made from natural fabrics cut for maneuverability, like a long denim jumper dress worn over a shirt of pure white cotton. God would look, in other words, like Maya Rudolph running errands on a Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/magazine/16mag-rudolph1-copy/16mag-rudolph1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 761, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/16/magazine/16mag-rudolph1-copy/16mag-rudolph1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 761}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/magazine/16mag-rudolph1-copy/16mag-rudolph1-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 807, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/magazine/16mag-rudolph1-copy/16mag-rudolph1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1614, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'capt