nmar’s government defends the harsh sentence given to two courageous reporters who exposed mass murder, it breaks a fundamental promise of democracy: the rule of law based on facts. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/16/opinion/16Adler.html', 'snippet': 'When Myanmar’s government defends the harsh sentence given to two courageous reporters who exposed mass murder, it breaks a fundamental promise of democracy: the rule of law based on facts. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Myanmar, as everywhere, facts have power. It was the gruesome facts uncovered by two of our reporters for Reuters, Wa Lone and Kyaw Soe Oo, that led to their being framed, arrested, tried and — this month — handed a draconian seven-year prison sentence. Last week, Myanmar’s civilian leader, Daw Aung San Suu Kyi, resolutely ignored the facts and vigorously defended the unjust convictions. With the United Nations General Assembly gathering soon, it’s time to harness the facts to secure our reporters’ freedom.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16Adler1A/16Adler1A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16Adler1A/16Adler1A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16Adler1A/16Adler1A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16Adler1A/16Adler1A-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16Adler1A/16Adler1A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16Adler1A/16Adler1A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16Adler1A/16Adler1A-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Myanmar’s Assault on a Truthful Press', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Myanmar’s Assault on a Truthful Press', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rohingya (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reuters Group PLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aung San Suu Kyi', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-16T23:10:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen J. Adler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Adler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b7cecf4-f43b-5539-b4f9-f0fd3ae2eb47', 'word_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b7cecf4-f43b-5539-b4f9-f0fd3ae2eb47'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Sale and Jacob deGrom took the mound in what could have been a tantalizing matchup. But Sale is coming off an injury, and deGrom’s Mets are far from the playoffs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/16/sports/baseball/degrom-sale-mets-red-sox.html', 'snippet': 'Chris Sale and Jacob deGrom took the mound in what could have been a tantalizing matchup. But Sale is coming off an injury, and deGrom’s Mets are far from the playoffs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — On Sept. 11, 1985, two standout pitchers, Dwight Gooden of the Mets and John Tudor of the St. Louis Cardinals, faced off at Shea Stadium in a matchup for the ages. Gooden fired nine scoreless innings; Tudor threw 10. The Cardinals won, 1-0, in the 10th inning when Cesar Cedeno smashed a home run off Jesse Orosco.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/17/sports/17metsweb/merlin_143830599_d53406bc-7d26-47a0-9bce-10b29942c334-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/17/sports/17metsweb/merlin_143830599_d53406bc-7d26-47a0-9bce-10b29942c334-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/17/sports/17metsweb/merlin_143830599_d53406bc-7d26-47a0-9bce-10b29942c334-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/17/sports/17metsweb/merlin_143830599_d53406bc-7d26-47a0-9bce-10b29942c334-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/