8/09/16/opinion/columnists/democrats-midterms-progressive-left-trump.html', 'snippet': 'And the Democratic Party has not actually become a band of radical leftists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Conventional wisdom says that the middle is disappearing from American politics: The Republicans have moved far to the right, the Democrats far to the left, and woe to any moderate voters looking for politicians to represent their views.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16leonhardt-web/merlin_140389425_c167857c-8bfe-43f1-9431-c302d9c27db2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16leonhardt-web/merlin_140389425_c167857c-8bfe-43f1-9431-c302d9c27db2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16leonhardt-web/merlin_140389425_c167857c-8bfe-43f1-9431-c302d9c27db2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16leonhardt-web/merlin_140389425_c167857c-8bfe-43f1-9431-c302d9c27db2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16leonhardt-web/16leonhardt-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16leonhardt-web/16leonhardt-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/16leonhardt-web/16leonhardt-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Trump Derangement Syndrome’ Is a Myth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Trump Derangement Syndrome’ is a Myth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2018)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Impeachment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Socialism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-16T23:41:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Columnists', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f86a4b97-fd33-5f2b-a854-af83ce8cae6c', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f86a4b97-fd33-5f2b-a854-af83ce8cae6c'}, {'abstract': 'In a rematch of last year’s A.F.C. Championship Game, Jacksonville built a large lead and held strong down the stretch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/16/sports/jaguars-patriots.html', 'snippet': 'In a rematch of last year’s A.F.C. Championship Game, Jacksonville built a large lead and held strong down the stretch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JACKSONVILLE, Fla. — Really, this was not about revenge for the Jaguars, because in no way could a Week 2 victory in dryer-vent conditions here negate a season-ending defeat absorbed amid the New England winter, nor could it erase eight months of frustration, nor retroactively award them a conference title, and the Super Bowl appearance they still covet.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/17/sports/17patriots-bortles/merlin_143848818_c33e38dc-b499-493a-9146-a14e8b444417-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 472, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/17/sports/17patriots-bortles/merlin_143848818_c33e38dc-b499-493a-9146-a14e8b444417-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 472}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/17/sports/17patriots-bortles/merlin_143848818_c33e38dc-b499-493a-9146-a14e8b444417-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 805, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/17/sports/17patriots-bortles/merlin_143848818_c33e38dc-b499-493a-9146-a14e8b444417-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1610, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/17/sports/17patriots-bortles/17patriots-bortles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/17/sports/17patriots-bortles/17patriots-bortles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/17/sports/17patriots-bortles/17patriots-bortles-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jaguars Stifle Patriots, and This Time There’s No Comeback', 'kicker': 'Jaguars 31, Patriots 20', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bold Rebuttal,  If Not Revenge,  By the Jaguars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jacksonville Jaguars', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bortles, Blake (1992- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marrone, Doug', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-16T23:50:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3820d1c1-254f-51bb-9032-2f032e4424a5', 'word_count': 982, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3820d1c1-254f-51bb-9032-2f032e4424a5'}, {'abstract': 'The storied weekly spent less than a year as part of the Iowa-based Meredith Corporation. Its new owners, Mr. Benioff and his wife, are buying it for $190 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/16/business/dealbook/time-magazine-salesforce-marc-benioff.html', 'snippet': 'The storied weekly spent le