nal': 'By Bruce Fretts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fretts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a057259-8519-5f83-a024-c60252875820', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a057259-8519-5f83-a024-c60252875820'}, {'abstract': 'Pastry chefs in the United States are exploring the countless possibilities of kakigori, a traditional dessert that’s both exacting and amenable to interpretation. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/17/dining/kakigori-japanese-shave-ice.html', 'snippet': 'Pastry chefs in the United States are exploring the countless possibilities of kakigori, a traditional dessert that’s both exacting and amenable to interpretation. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Norie Uematsu became a pastry chef, she waited all year for shave-ice season at home in Japan. Now, she decides when that season begins and ends.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/19/dining/19shave2/merlin_143382264_dcc863f9-a3e4-4a92-8bcc-5997c077a6cc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/19/dining/19shave2/merlin_143382264_dcc863f9-a3e4-4a92-8bcc-5997c077a6cc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/19/dining/19shave2/merlin_143382264_dcc863f9-a3e4-4a92-8bcc-5997c077a6cc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/19/dining/19shave2/merlin_143382264_dcc863f9-a3e4-4a92-8bcc-5997c077a6cc