ganization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/594d1cc6-7cd6-5a59-b268-618b99fba703', 'word_count': 1212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/594d1cc6-7cd6-5a59-b268-618b99fba703'}, {'abstract': 'The Missouri senator is in a neck-and-neck race to keep a crucial seat in Democratic hands, facing criticism from her opponent that she’s a Washington insider.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/18/us/politics/mccaskill-missouri-midterms.html', 'snippet': 'The Missouri senator is in a neck-and-neck race to keep a crucial seat in Democratic hands, facing criticism from her opponent that she’s a Washington insider.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORTAGEVILLE, Mo. — Senator Claire McCaskill had rolled through miles of cotton and soybean fields, heading deep into enemy territory — Missouri’s Bootheel, Trump Country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/us/politics/00mccaskill1/merlin_143134626_7fd660ed-8d45-447d-b6fe-6361c4248be0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/14/us/politics/00mccaskill1/merlin_143134626_7fd660ed-8d45-447d-b6fe-6361c4248be0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/us/politics/00mccaskill1/merlin_143134626_7fd660ed-8d45-447d-b6fe-6361c4248be0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/us/politics/00mccaskill1/merlin_143134626_7fd660ed-8d45-447d-b6fe-6361c4248be0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/us/politics/00mccaskill1/00mccaskill1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/14/us/politics/00mccaskill1/00mccaskill1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/us/politics/00mccaskill1/00mccaskill1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Claire McCaskill Is in a Rugged Political Fight. She’s Survived Them Before.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Missouri Race, McCaskill Says, ‘Everything Has to Go Well’ ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCaskill, Claire', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawley, Josh D (1979- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-18T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Saul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d659346-6d3b-5e31-a3ed-4903e791abe4', 'word_count': 1701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d659346-6d3b-5e31-a3ed-4903e791abe4'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/18/books/review/new-noteworthy-jason-stallman.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KAFKAESQUE By Peter Kuper and Franz Kafka. (Norton, $19.95.) Kuper has been adapting Kafka’s stories in graphic novel form since 1988. This book gathers 14 of them, including “In the Penal Colony” and “A Hunger Artist,” placing the work in a contemporary setting so that Kafka, that master critic of the modern world, can comment on issues like civil rights and homelessness. STAN SMITH By Stan Smith, foreword by Pharrell Williams. (Rizzoli, $55.) The Stan Smith tennis sneaker, named after the former world No. 1 tennis player Stan Smith, has maintained cult status since it was first introduced over four decades ago. This book celebrates the sneaker’s reach, from mentions in rap lyrics to its appearance in Bollywood movies. THE WHITE HORSE By Mary McCartney. (Rizzoli, $55.) McCartney, a photographer who grew up in the Sussex countryside, focuses here on one white stallion, Alejandro, and the intimate relationship between horse and rider. WRITERS UNDER SURVEILLANCE Edited by JPat Brown, B. C. D. Lipton and Michael Morisy. (MIT Press, paper, $24.95.) Obtained through the Freedom of Information Act, the F.B.I. files in this collection monitor writers considered by the government to have been subversives. Many of the intellectual heavyweights are here, from Hannah Arendt to Susan Sontag to James Baldwin. AMY WINEHOUSE Photographs by Blake Wood, text by Nancy Jo Sales. (Taschen, $40.) Wood’s images of the singer, especially of her relaxing on the beach at St. Lucia, show a human, private side to contrast the self-destructive public persona.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/23/books/review/23NewNoteworthy0/23NewNoteworthy0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/23/books/review/23NewNoteworthy0/23NewNoteworthy0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/23/books/review/23NewNoteworthy0/23NewNoteworthy0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/23/books/review/23NewNoteworthy0/23NewNoteworthy0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1056, 'width': 1640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/23/books/review/23NewNoteworthy0/23NewNoteworthy0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/23/books/review/23NewNoteworthy0/23NewNoteworthy0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/23/books/review/23NewNoteworthy0/23NewNoteworthy0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New & Noteworthy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New &amp; Noteworthy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank'