 'Yet again, the nonconformist rebels of yesteryear become the standard-setters of today. The Museum of Modern Art exhibition “Judson Dance Theater: The Work Is Never Done” shows why the work of the New York downtown dance experimentalists of the 1960s was once radical. Many people would still be challenged by it today.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/19/arts/19rainer-1/merlin_143892762_be861356-287c-40a8-9ad9-c67ba73905f8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/19/arts/19rainer-1/merlin_143892762_be861356-287c-40a8-9ad9-c67ba73905f8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/19/arts/19rainer-1/merlin_143892762_be861356-287c-40a8-9ad9-c67ba73905f8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/19/arts/19rainer-1/merlin_143892762_be861356-287c-40a8-9ad9-c67ba73905f8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1357, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/19/arts/19rainer-1/19rainer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/19/arts/19rainer-1/19rainer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/19/arts/19rainer-1/19rainer-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: The Humanity of Yvonne Rainer’s Natural and Peculiar Dances', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Natural and Peculiar Come in From the ’60s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Judson Dance Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rainer, Yvonne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Trio A (Dance)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-18T17:58:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/09cb0740-6549-5d27-9864-449df08813df', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09cb0740-6549-5d27-9864-449df08813df'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists are focusing on a relatively small number of human genes and neglecting thousands of others. The reasons have more to do with professional survival than genetics. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/18/science/why-your-dna-is-still-uncharted-territory.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists are focusing on a relatively small number of human genes and neglecting thousands of others. The reasons have more to do with professional survival than genetics. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'You have a gene called PNMA6F. All people do, but no one knows the purpose of that gene or the protein it makes. And as it turns out, PNMA6F has a lot of company in t