middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/474dec2d-85ee-521b-b584-fa667f680077', 'word_count': 1648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/474dec2d-85ee-521b-b584-fa667f680077'}, {'abstract': 'He has helmed the house founded by his grandmother for 40 years. Here, he shares his many inspirations with T.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/19/t-magazine/albert-kriemler-akris-profile-in-style.html', 'snippet': 'He has helmed the house founded by his grandmother for 40 years. Here, he shares his many inspirations with T.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I grew up to the steady hum of sewing machines,” says Albert Kriemler, the creative director of his family’s 96-year-old company, Akris. Founded in 1922 by his grandmother, Alice Kriemler-Schoch (the company’s name is a sort of acronym of her initials), the Swiss label got its start making polka-dotted aprons in the alpine town of St. Gallen, famous for its embroidery, where the brand’s headquarters are still located. In the ’60s and ’70s, Kriemler’s parents, Max and Ute, expanded Akris’s scope, producing prêt-à-porter for such houses as Ted Lapidus and Givenchy. As a young man, Kriemler would often travel to fabric fairs with his family; on a trip to Paris in 1976, he attended his first Yves Saint Laurent show. “It was then that I knew I was completely infatuated with fashion,” he says. He made plans to study at Paris’s École de la Chambre Syndicale de la Couture, but they were waylaid when, after Akris’s managing director died suddenly, Kriemler’s father convinced him to join the business as creative director in 1980. He was just 19.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 749}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 821, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1662, 'width': 1332, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS/06tmag-kreimler-slide-O8XS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Exacting Eye of Akris’s Albert Kriemler', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Akris (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', '