 2014, Tom Perry drove his truck out to the end of Virginia’s State Route 695 and found himself at the edge of Windmill Point. This is a remote peninsula, mostly undeveloped, where the waters of the Rappahannock River and the Chesapeake Bay meet. He couldn’t get to where he was going by car, so he carried his kayak over the beach grass and set out into the water. As he turned the corner of the Point, he could see the place he’d come to find, the shallow waters running along a stretch of quiet beach spotted with dead scraggly trees.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '150', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/t-magazine/oakImage-1536957949857/oakImage-1536957949857-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/14/t-magazine/oakImage-1536957949857/oakImage-1536957949857-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/t-magazine/oakImage-1536957949857/oakImage-1536957949857-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/t-magazine/oakImage-1536957949857/oakImage-1536957949857-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1490, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/t-magazine/oakImage-1536957949857/oakImage-1536957949857-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/14/t-magazine/oakImage-1536957949857/oakImage-1536957949857-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbn