ance Theater: The Work Is Never Done.” In Gene Friedman’s 1964 film “3 Dances,” bodies aren’t just moving through space: They’re also speaking to the breadth and possibility of the art form. Judson Dance Theater, the daring 1960s collective, taught the world that a dance is not just one thing. A stage is not just one thing. And anybody, with any body, can dance.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/21/arts/21judson-moma1/merlin_143937357_e2ee6aad-8d04-4e25-a779-abb552cd7250-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/21/arts/21judson-moma1/merlin_143937357_e2ee6aad-8d04-4e25-a779-abb552cd7250-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/21/arts/21judson-moma1/merlin_143937357_e2ee6aad-8d04-4e25-a779-abb552cd7250-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/21/arts/21judson-moma1/merlin_143937357_e2ee6aad-8d04-4e25-a779-abb552cd7250-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1385, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/21/arts/21judson-moma1/21judson-moma1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/21/arts/21judson-moma1/21judson-moma1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/21/arts/21judson-moma1/21judson-moma1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: MoMA Puts Judson Dance on Display and, Better Yet, in Motion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance on Display, and in Motion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Judson Dance Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Forti, Simone', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rainer, Yvonne', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rauschenberg, Robert', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneemann, Carolee', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halprin, Anna', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hay, Deborah', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Trio A (Dance)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Judson Dance Theater: The Work Is Never Done (Exhibit)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-20T14:59:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dfa9bca-e9eb-5c87-a69f-5024ec48d216', 'word_count': 1399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dfa9bca-e9eb-5c87-a69f-5024ec48d216'}, {'abstract': 'T’s cultural compendium of what’s new.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/20/t-magazine/aman-skincare-luigi-caccia-dominioni-bb-italia-news.html', 'snippet': 'T’s cultural compendium of what’s new.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Resourcefulness” is not a word one immediately associates with high fashion. Yet patchwork and quilting — homespun, traditionally feminine crafts that in times past transformed worn-out clothes or leftover bits of fabric into things beautiful, useful and warm — are having a moment on the runway. At the fall shows, Dior sent out dresses, jackets and even boots in crazy quilt patterns. Missoni upcycled vintage swatches into a kaleidoscopic coat, and Etro combined a “Little House on the Prairie” aesthetic with eclectic geometries. At Calvin Klein, Raf Simons paid homage to the American heartland with hand-sewn chiffon dresses inspired by vintage quilts. No mere exercise in nostalgia, the collection also struck a dystopian note: Some of the models wore hand-knit balaclavas and clutched Mylar-backed blankets, refugees from a strangely luxurious, survivalist future.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ppt-slide-B2YZ/05tmag-ppt-slide-B2YZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ppt-slide-B2YZ/05tmag-ppt-slide-B2YZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 613}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ppt-slide-B2YZ/05tmag-ppt-slide-B2YZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 794, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ppt-slide-B2YZ/05tmag-ppt-slide-B2YZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 794, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0