': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-21T22:15:21+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6217a432-7158-54db-85fd-06b0aad20563', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6217a432-7158-54db-85fd-06b0aad20563'}, {'abstract': 'Luke and Lucie Meier, the brand’s husband-and-wife creative directors, prepare for their show during Milan Fashion Week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/21/t-magazine/luke-lucie-meier-jil-sander.html', 'snippet': 'Luke and Lucie Meier, the brand’s husband-and-wife creative directors, prepare for their show during Milan Fashion Week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s the proof of a happy marriage? For Luke and Lucie Meier, the husband-and-wife design duo at the helm of the Jil Sander brand, it’s that they still want to have coffee together before it’s time to go to work. This week, just one day before their spring 2019 fashion show, the pair left their Milan apartment and crossed the street to the elegantly antique Marchesi pastry shop (founding date: 1824) for a caffè macchiato each, and a fresh grapefruit juice for Lucie. “This is how we start every day,” says Luke.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/21/t-magazine/fashion/jil-sander-slide-G3HS/jil-sander-slide-G3HS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/21/t-magazine/fashion/jil-sander-slide-G3HS/jil-sander-slide-G3HS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/21/t-magazine/fashion/jil-sander-slide-G3HS/jil-sander-slide-G3HS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683