ect', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Socialists of America', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-22T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maggie Astor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maggie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Astor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/b50a5c09-ea0f-565f-b5d5-88f5e60558c9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/b50a5c09-ea0f-565f-b5d5-88f5e60558c9'}, {'abstract': 'A team of New York Times journalists went door to door in Punta Santiago, visiting 163 homes. Here’s a dramatic visual presentation of what they found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/22/us/photos-hurricane-maria-puerto-rico.html', 'snippet': 'A team of New York Times journalists went door to door in Punta Santiago, visiting 163 homes. Here’s a dramatic visual presentation of what they found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In August, a team of New York Times journalists visited Punta Santiago, a small town in Puerto Rico near where Hurricane Maria made landfall one year ago. We documented the damage that remains from the storm in more than 150 homes. Many are living in ruin a year later, still awaiting repairs. In house after house, it looks like the hurricane just hit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/21/us/prstub/merlin_144033363_2be93a9a-822a-4cd0-b20a-7148a24ff7c6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/21/us/prstub/merlin_1440