ticle', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rodrigo Zeidan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rodrigo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeidan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e021d83-5205-53d8-80a0-fb616e4dfb12', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e021d83-5205-53d8-80a0-fb616e4dfb12'}, {'abstract': 'In Puerto Rico, communities are still reeling from the destruction of Hurricane Maria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/22/opinion/sunday/back-from-the-storm.html', 'snippet': 'In Puerto Rico, communities are still reeling from the destruction of Hurricane Maria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last October, my sister and I traveled to Puerto Rico to pick up our 89-year-old mother and take her back to New York. Hurricane Maria had battered her remote mountain community in Río Grande, near the El Yunque National Forest.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/23/opinion/sunday/23Exposures1/merlin_144088050_9a1be8d0-931d-4017-a0c4-d1ee09b2a589-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/23/opinion/sunday/23Exposures1/merlin_144088050_9a1be8d0-931d-4017-a0c4-d1ee09b2a589-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/23/opinion/sunday/23Exposures1/merlin_144088050_9a1be8d0-931d-4017-a0c4-d1ee09b2a589-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/