e get? Episode 9 of our video series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We commoners have always had an ambivalent relationship with celebrities. We admire them, and we resent them. We want to be more like them, and we want them to be more like us. We want to somehow close the gap between them, the stars that produce culture, and us, the audiences who consume it. Now the internet has given us unprecedented tools to exert control over celebrities, in increasingly creepy and invasive ways. Take on Hollywood with “Internetting” Episode 9.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/24/autossell/rebeccablackv2/rebeccablackv2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/24/autossell/rebeccablackv2/rebeccablackv2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/24/autossell/rebeccablackv2/rebeccablackv2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/24/autossell/rebeccablackv2/rebeccablackv2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/24/autossell/rebeccablackv2/rebeccablackv2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/24/autossell/rebeccablackv2/rebeccablackv2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/24/autossell/rebeccablackv2/rebeccablackv2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Control a Celebrity Like a Puppet', 'kicker': 'INTERNETTING WITH AMANDA HESS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Control A Celebrity Like A Puppet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cameo (Mobile App)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-24T09:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Hess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5043484a-6e07-5082-a377-aaebd0a84b1b', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5043484a-6e07-5082-a377-aaebd0a84b1b'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks to the internet — and RuPaul — what was once a queer subculture has gone totally mainstream. Episode 8 of our video series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/24/arts/drag-queens-internet.html', 'snippet': 'Thanks to the internet — and RuPaul — what was once a queer subculture has gone totally mainstream. Episode 8 of our video series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may know him as the editor of “Internetting.” Or as the charming man who appears at my side at the end of the videos. Or as the owner of “Internetting” feline correspondent Wanda. This week, he is also your host: Shane O’Neill is taking over for his very own episode. It’s about how the internet is changing drag performance, and what happens when an art form created by a marginalized community goes mainstream. Welcome to Shane Week.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/05/arts/9_Drag_New/9_Drag_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/10/05/arts/9_Drag_New/9_Drag_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/05/arts/9_Drag_New/9_Drag_New-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/05/arts/9_Drag_New/9_Drag_New-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/05/arts/9_Drag_New/9_Drag_New-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/10/05/arts/9_Drag_New/9_Drag_New-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/05/arts/9_Drag_New/9_Drag_New-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Drag Survive the Internet?', 'kicker': 'INTERNETTING WITH AMANDA HESS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can Drag Survive The Internet?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-24T09:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': "By Amanda Hess and Shane O'Neill", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Shane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Neill", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bcbb12e-9ef8-5738-ab2a-399f533c4312', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bcbb12e-9ef8-5738-ab2a-399f533c4312'}, {'abstract': 'Those romantic, heartwarming surprise proposal videos are actually the worst. Episode 10 of our video series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/24/arts/surprise-proposal-videos.html', 'snippet': 'Those romantic, heartwarming surprise proposal videos are actually the worst. Episode 10 of our video series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YouTube loves a surprise. So much viral video content is built on just sneaking up on people with an extravagant display of good news: Proposal videos, promposal videos, college acceptance videos, soldier homecoming videos. The genre is so emotionally powerful, it can even become a little bit manipulative — working to make us believe stuff we don’t actually agree with. Get taken by surprise in “Internetting” Episode 10.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/11_Surprise_New/11_Surprise_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/11_Surprise_New/11_Surprise_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/11_Surprise_New/11_Surprise_New-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/11_Surprise_New/11_Surprise_New-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/11_Surprise_New/11_Surprise_New-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/11_Surprise_New/11_Surprise_New-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/11_Surprise_New/11_Surprise_New-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Hate Proposal Videos. Here’s Why I’m Right.', 'kicker': 'INTERNETTING WITH AMANDA HESS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Hate Proposal Videos. Here’s Why I’m Right.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-24T09:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Hess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': 