inorities in each tribal homeland. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/24/opinion/south-sudan-peace-agreement.html', 'snippet': 'The agreement will divide the country into a collection of tribes and disenfranchise minorities in each tribal homeland. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sept. 12, Salva Kiir, the president of South Sudan, and his major adversary, the former vice-president and rebel leader Riek Machar, signed a peace agreement in Addis Ababa, the capital of Ethiopia — the 12th agreement between them — to end the long, brutal civil war that has killed thousands and displaced millions in South Sudan since December 2013.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/24/opinion/24mamdani1/merlin_142072095_0f07af33-e6a9-4a22-8a00-c07091a494cc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/24/opinion/24mamdani1/merlin_142072095_0f07af33-e6a9-4a22-8a00-c07091a494cc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/24/opinion/24mamdani1/merlin_142072095_0f07af33-e6a9-4a22-8a00-c07091a494cc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/24/opinion/24mamdani1/merlin_142072095_0f07af33-e6a9-4a22-8a00-c07091a494cc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/24/opinion/24mamdani1/24mamdani1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2