gelin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teshigawara, Saburo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hervieu, Dominique', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadj, Josef', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dan, Madalina', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Siniarska, Agata', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merzouki, Mourad', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-24T15:28:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d69935ab-a1c3-53a5-b30b-b1f865f287c6', 'word_count': 1127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d69935ab-a1c3-53a5-b30b-b1f865f287c6'}, {'abstract': 'West 32 Reserve, named after Koreatown in Manhattan, is meant for sipping, but plays nicely in a martini.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/24/dining/drinks/west-32-soju.html', 'snippet': 'West 32 Reserve, named after Koreatown in Manhattan, is meant for sipping, but plays nicely in a martini.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Lee introduced soju, the popular Korean spirit, to his friend at George Washington University, Maxwell Fine, some time ago in New York. The two decided to make their own without artificial sweeteners and other additives, as a sideline to their day jobs in finance and law. Named for the Manhattan block known as Koreatown, they introduced their West 32 Soju in early 2017. It’s a light (at 19.9 percent alcohol), pleasant soju, distilled from a corn base and sweetened with cane sugar in Clifton Park, N.Y., near Albany. A new reserve version, aged in white oak bourbon barrels, is stronger (at 32 percent alcohol), pale straw in color, with the aromas of vanilla and freshly mowed hay. Though easy to drink straight, a splash of it does nice things when substituted for vermouth in a martini.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/26/dining/26burner5/merlin_144061209_82c2d9f9-4241-4784-8ceb-07739a2bae84-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/26/dining/26burner5/merlin_144061209_82c2d9f9-4241-4784-8ceb-07739a2bae84-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 766}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/26/dining/26burner5/merlin_144061209_82c2d9f9-4241-4784-8ceb-07739a2bae84-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 803, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/26/dining/26burner5/merlin_144061209_82c2d9f9-4241-4784-8ceb-07739a2bae84-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1606, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/26/dining/26burner5/26burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/26/dining/26burner5/26burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/26/dining/26burner5/26burner5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Soju, Straight From New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sip: Soju, Straight  From New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liquor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-24T15:49:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Wine, Beer & Cocktails', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/919c10c0-8561-533f-93d8-df7a616c2411', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/919c10c0-8561-533f-93d8-df7a616c2411'}, {'abstract': 'A Japanese billionaire, Yusaku Maezawa, wants artists to join him on a pioneering spaceflight. We asked some leading candidates about the idea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/24/arts/design/artists-moon-spacex.html', 'snippet': 'A Japanese billionaire, Yusaku Maezawa, wants artists to join him on a pioneering spaceflight. We asked some leading candidates about the idea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Its ambition is to “revolutionize space travel,” but when it comes to manned missions, Elon Musk’s SpaceX company sometimes seems to have struggled to … well, to get off the ground. It’s become a major player in satellite launches, and achieved some impressive milestones, but some of the targets and timelines related to its grandest plans have turned out to be wildly optimistic. That’s not even to mention the Tesla chief executive’s recent behavior, which has led some investors to question exactly which planet he is on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/25/world/25moonartists/merlin_143910663_7f9cbda3-bb63-409d-8015-fb9dc5c57256-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 414, 'width': 600, 'subType'