e, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ogrodnek, Joseph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Floret (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Foods', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ace Hotel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-25T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Priya Krishna', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Priya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krishna', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55538112-45a8-5a95-bc97-727785e72389', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55538112-45a8-5a95-bc97-727785e72389'}, {'abstract': 'Ian Buruma’s exit from The New York Review of Books threatens to inhibit our intellectual culture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/25/opinion/ian-buruma-jian-ghomeshi.html', 'snippet': 'Ian Buruma’s exit from The New York Review of Books threatens to inhibit our intellectual culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Robert B. Silvers, the founding editor of The New York Review of Books, published an article in late 2011 speculating that Dominique Strauss-Kahn, a prominent French politician accused of sexually assaulting a hotel housekeeper in New York, might have been set up, I remember being shocked and appalled. If you accepted the evidence that the author, Edward Jay Epstein, had amassed (timeline inconsistencies, missing cellphones), you had to conclude that the accuser wasn’t just lying, she was also collaborating with nefarious entities to bring down Mr. Strauss-Kahn, who happened to be planning a presidential run in France.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/25BURUMA/merlin_143984895_fd62485f-2a5e-4b93-a9a4-6dd513db202e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/25BURUMA/merlin_143984895_fd62485f-2a5e-4b93-a9a4-6dd513db202e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/25BURUMA/merlin_143984895_fd62485f-2a5e-4b93-a9a4-6dd513db202e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/25BURUMA/merlin_143984895_fd62485f-2a5e-4b93-a9a4-6dd513db202e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/25BURUMA/25BURUMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/25BURUMA/25BURUMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/25/arts/25BURUMA/25BURUMA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Perils of Publishing in a #MeToo Moment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [