48, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/reader-center/26readers-cosby2/merlin_144234639_656950ce-f516-4b58-b1cc-444d5eccff60-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/27/reader-center/26readers-cosby2/merlin_144234639_656950ce-f516-4b58-b1cc-444d5eccff60-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/reader-center/26readers-cosby2/merlin_144234639_656950ce-f516-4b58-b1cc-444d5eccff60-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cosby Sentenced as Brett Kavanaugh Battles Accusations. And It’s Only Tuesday.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cosby, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kavanaugh, Brett M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '#MeToo Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-25T16:25:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NewsDesk', 'section_name': 'Reader Center', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lela Moore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f36b7628-c44e-5dd6-a2e4-a1d31dbaa522', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f36b7628-c44e-5dd6-a2e4-a1d31dbaa522'}, {'abstract': 'Middle Eastern food on the Upper West Side, a Randalls Island cafe from the team at Untamed Sandwiches, and more restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/25/dining/nyc-restaurant-openings.html', 'snippet': 'Middle Eastern food on the Upper West Side, a Randalls Island cafe from the team at Untamed Sandwiches, and more restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A makeover is nothing short of perfect for Antoni Porowski, the food and wine maven for Netflix’s “Queer Eye,” a show all about new beginnings. He has taken over what was once the Village Den in the West Village, and with his partners, the restaurateurs Lisle Richards and Eric Marx, he has turned a former 36-year-old diner into a fast-casual, all-day cafe that’s very today. Describing the food, which Mr. Porowski oversees, as “healthy offerings,” Mr. Richards said it was vegetable-forward and free of gluten, soy and red meat. The cafe serves breakfast (avocado tartine, almond and walnut pancakes), salads (almond Caesar; grilled chicken with spinach, egg and green goddess dressing), bowls (honey-roasted turkey meatballs over cauliflower rice), and a long list of smoothie options. They’re also serving what they call TV Dinners, a meat-and-two featuring stuffed cabbage with pine nuts and macadamia-crusted fish sticks, among other proteins, with a choice of a dozen sides. The place is done in white, with lots of decorative light wood scaffolding and greenery. A clever, cartoonish mural of the West Village covers one wall. There is no waiter service. (Opens Monday)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/26/dining/26OFF/merlin_144097671_2dd0c41f-302f-46f2-ae02-18cec1122917-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/26/dining/26OFF/merlin_144097671_2dd0c41f-302f-46f2-ae02-18cec1122917-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'cr