, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8795fd95-0c90-50aa-bd91-cd4cb8cb1ce3', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8795fd95-0c90-50aa-bd91-cd4cb8cb1ce3'}, {'abstract': 'Nghia Pho, 68, hoping to win a promotion at the National Security Agency, started taking his classified work home, where Russian hackers are believed to have stolen it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/25/us/politics/nghia-pho-nsa-prison-sentence.html', 'snippet': 'Nghia Pho, 68, hoping to win a promotion at the National Security Agency, started taking his classified work home, where Russian hackers are believed to have stolen it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — As a Vietnamese immigrant with imperfect English, Nghia H. Pho felt he was falling behind his fellow National Security Agency software developers in promotions and pay. So in 2010, after four years on the job, he began taking highly classified documents to his Maryland home to get extra work done at night and on weekends in an effort to improve his performance evaluations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/26/us/politics/26dc-nsa/26dc-nsa-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/26/us/politics/26dc-nsa/26dc-nsa-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/26/us/politics/26dc-nsa/26dc-nsa-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/26/us/politics/26dc-nsa/26dc-nsa-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank':