aterial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d12e382d-e9d1-5e50-bb5a-aacfa357f54b', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d12e382d-e9d1-5e50-bb5a-aacfa357f54b'}, {'abstract': 'Roller skates have become an accessory of female empowerment. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/style/roller-skates.html', 'snippet': 'Roller skates have become an accessory of female empowerment. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once, roller skating was a family-friendly activity. At the height of the roller skating craze, during the 1970s and ’80s, you went to the roller rink and banged your feet against the wood while dancing to “Don’t Bring Me Down” by Electric Light Orchestra. Or maybe you went to the local theater just to stare in wonder at Linda Blair in “Roller Boogie,” wishing that one day you too could find love on the trashy Venice Beach boardwalk. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/fashion/27rollerskates1/merlin_143880396_7901b9d7-207e-4ebf-a7b4-2631017a62ec-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/27/fashion/27rollerskates1/merlin_143880396_7901b9d7-207e-4ebf-a7b4-2631017a62ec-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/fashion/27rollerskates1/merlin_143880396_7901b9d7-207e-4ebf-a7b4-2631017a62ec-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/fashion/27rollerskates1/merlin_143880396_7901b9d7-207e-4ebf-a7b4-2631017a62ec-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/fashion/27rollerskates1/00rollerskates1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/27/fashion/27rollerskates1/00rollerskates1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/fashion/27rollerskates1/00rollerskates1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wheel Thing', 'kicker': 'cultural studies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Feminism On Skates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roller Skating', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-26T09:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hayley Krischer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hayley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krischer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/add968b3-8819-5d5b-8cf1-120116b3887c', 'word_count': 1392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/add968b3-8819-5d5b-8cf1-120116b3887c'}, {'abstract': 'As the midterms approach, America’s electronic voting systems are more vulnerable than ever. Why isn’t anyone trying to fix them?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/magazine/election-security-crisis-midterms.html', 'snippet': 'As the midterms approach, America’s electronic voting systems are more vulnerable than ever. Why isn’t anyone trying to fix them?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was mid-July 2016 when Neil Jenkins learned that someone had hacked the Illinois Board of Elections. Jenkins was a director in the Office of Cybersecurity and Communications at the Department of Homeland Security, the domestic agency with a congressional mandate to protect “critical infrastructure.” Although election systems were not yet formally designated as such — that wouldn’t happen until January 2017 — it was increasingly clear that the presidential election was becoming a national-security issue. Just a month before, Americans had been confronted with the blockbuster revelation that Russian government actors had hacked the Democratic National Committee’s servers and stolen private email and opposition research against Donald Trump, the Republican presidential candidate.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '39', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Hacking-promo/30Mag-Hacking-1-articleLarge-v2.gif', 'height': 733, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Hacking-promo/30Mag-Hacking-1-articleLarge-v2.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 733}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Hacking-promo/30Mag-Hacking-1-jumbo-v2.gif', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Hacking-promo/30Mag-Hacking-1-superJumbo-v2.gif', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1676, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Hacking-promo/30Mag-Hacking-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Hacking-promo/30Mag-Hacking-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Hacking-promo/30Mag-Hacking-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Crisis of Election Security', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Crisis of Election Security', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2018)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare and Defense', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Machines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-26T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Zetter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zetter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76d56774-1e08-5660-808c-d6f6ff205366', 'word_count': 6530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76d56774-1e08-5660-808c-d6f6ff205366'}, {'abstract': 'A referendum on the November ballot in Florida would re-enfranchise 1.5 million citizens — and could change the state’s electorate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/magazine/ex-felons-voting-rights-florida.html', 'snippet': 'A referendum on the November ballot in Florida would re-enfranchise 1.5 million citizens — and could change the state’s electorate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty-five years ago, when he was a sophomore at Ohio State, Neil Volz started volunteering for his state senator, Bob Ney. Volz grew up in a family that wasn’t especially political, but he was drawn to libertarian principles about limited regulation and taxation, and a political-science professor connected him with Ney, who was about to run in the Republican primary for an open seat in Congress. When Ney won his congressional election in 1994, the year Newt Gingrich’s “Republican revolution” swept Democrats from power in Washington, he asked Volz to join his staff. Volz was 24 (he had taken time off from college), and he decided to rent a car to drive to Washington and take the job. “It was a dream come true, honestly,” he told me.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-felon-slide-0R7E/30mag-felon-slide-0R7E-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-felon-slide-0R7E/30mag-felon-slide-0R7E-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-felon-slide-0R7E/30mag-felon-slide-0R7E-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-felon-slide-0R7E/30mag-felon-slide-0R7E-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption':