 'nyt://article/f0ca27e7-577a-526e-90c9-2ffd103444ca'}, {'abstract': 'For the chef Preeti Mistry, cooking is a way to express her complex perspective as a first-generation Indian-American.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/magazine/the-last-great-tomato-salad-of-the-year.html', 'snippet': 'For the chef Preeti Mistry, cooking is a way to express her complex perspective as a first-generation Indian-American.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Certain clichés, some more tenacious than others, define generations of Indian restaurants in the United States. It’s a font, the type stylized with curly, pointy-ended serifs. It’s a basket of cold, black-edged papad dressed up as bread service. Usually, though, it’s a menu of naan and curry, pleasing in its soft, warm vagueness. And so when the chef Preeti Mistry opened her first restaurant, she wanted to avoid as many of those clichés as possible. “I wanted to do something that was the opposite of all of that,” Mistry said. At first, she railed against naan and curry. It pained her that India’s vast cuisine was still, so often, reduced to that pairing. “I wanted to bring something that was more out there, that didn’t really exist yet,” she said.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-eat-alpha/30mag-eat-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 458, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-eat-alpha/30mag-eat-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 458}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-eat-alpha/30mag-eat-image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 782, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-eat-alpha/30mag-eat-image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1563, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-eat-alpha/30mag-eat-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-eat-alpha/30mag-eat-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-eat-alpha/30mag-eat-image1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Last Great Tomato Salad of the Year', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Last Great Tomato Salad of the Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salad Dressings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mistry, Preeti (Chef)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-26T12:52:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tejal Rao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tejal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d61f25e-262a-5ed3-b332-fbd67cc52043', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d61f25e-262a-5ed3-b332-fbd67cc52043'}, {'abstract': 'The writer and actor on HBO’s “Insecure” on rom-coms and black-girl magic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/magazine/natasha-rothwell-wants-to-be-a-romantic-lead.html', 'snippet': 'The writer and actor on HBO’s “Insecure” on rom-coms and black-girl magic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You’re a writer and an actor on HBO’s “Insecure,” which is now in its third season. Did you have any idea of how big the show would be when you first started working on it? I didn’t know just how much of a cultural phenomenon it would become. I just knew that, as a person of color, I had not seen these specific stories told before. When you think of “Girlfriends” or “Living Single” — they’re these extraordinary black women! But there are a lot of ordinary women who have ordinary problems. It’s not black-girl magic all the time — sometimes you don’t know where your wand is. You’re like, “Today I have no magic, and I have no money, and I just have to get through the day.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '74', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-talk-image2/30mag-talk-image2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-talk-image2/30mag-talk-image2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-talk-image2/30mag-talk-image2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-talk-image2/30mag-talk-image2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-talk-image2/30mag-talk-image2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-talk-image2/30mag-talk-image2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30mag-talk-image2/30mag-talk-image2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Natasha Rothwell Wants to Be a Romantic Lead', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Natasha Rothwell Wants to Be a Romantic Lead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-26T12:54:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Molly Lambert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Molly', 'lastname': 'Lambert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce012cd1-9c37-5c0e-bb74-70b7d9f68990', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce012cd1-9c37-5c0e-bb74-70b7d9f68990'}, {'abstract': 'Call, email, write, send pictures. Try to visit — but don’t harp when you do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/magazine/how-to-get-someone-out-of-a-cult.html', 'snippet': 'Call, email, write, send pictures. Try to visit — but don’t harp when you do.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Do everything you can to stay in touch,” says Janja Lalich, a sociology professor and consultant who studies cults and coercive influence and control. If you’re trying to persuade someone to leave a cult, supply reminders of the world beyond it by calling, emailing, writing letters, sending photographs and maybe even visiting, although Lalich warns that anyone can get lured into a cult. You should visit “only if you feel strong enough to resist,” she says.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Tip_1/30Mag-Tip_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Tip_1/30Mag-Tip_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Tip_1/30Mag-Tip_1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Tip_1/30Mag-Tip_1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1439, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Tip_1/30Mag-Tip_1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Tip_1/30Mag-Tip_1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/magazine/30Mag-Tip_1/30Mag-Tip_1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Get Someone Out of a Cult', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Get Someone Out of a Cult', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religious Cults', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-26T12:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58ba12e3-57b5-559b-8eb6-7cdab8d7ff19', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58ba12e3-57b5-559b-8eb6-7cdab8d7ff19'}, {'abstract': 'The timing is right for this feminist news sitcom, but the revival seems more interested in applause than laughs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/arts/television/murphy-brown-reboot-review.html', 'snippet': 'The timing is right for this feminist news sitcom, but the revival seems more interested in applause than laughs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Murphy Brown (Candice Bergen) walks back into Phil’s Bar (now run by Tyne Daly as Phil’s sister, Phyllis), the studio audience applauds. Why wouldn’t they? The original “Murphy Brown” was a cultural milestone, and Ms. Bergen’s acid performance as a brilliant, abrasive TV journalist was a classic of the form.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/arts/27murphybrown/27murphybrown-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/27/arts/27murphybrown/27murphybrow