 be the most southerly sighting of the Arctic species in British waters. Conservationists hope the animal will swim back to the ocean.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/world/europe/uk-beluga-whale-thames.html', 'snippet': 'It is said to be the most southerly sighting of the Arctic species in British waters. Conservationists hope the animal will swim back to the ocean.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Many remarkable things have emerged from the River Thames in its long, crowded and often filthy history, from pods of dolphins to unexploded World War II bombs. But few were as rare as the flash of pearly white spotted Tuesday afternoon near Coalhouse Fort, in a quiet stretch of the river in southeast England.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/world/27beluga/merlin_144306771_9a336c1e-89d2-4c9a-bbf1-f896ab3da9f3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/27/world/27beluga/merlin_144306771_9a336c1e-89d2-4c9a-bbf1-f896ab3da9f3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/world/27beluga/merlin_144306771_9a336c1e-89d2-4c9a-bbf1-f896ab3da9f3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/world/27beluga/merlin_144306771_9a336c1e-89d2-4c9a-bbf1-f896ab3da9f3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1175, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/world/27beluga/merlin_144306771_9a336c1e-89d2-4c9a