, 'headline': {'main': 'Uber Will Spend $10 Million to Solve a Problem It Helped Create', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uber to Spend $10 Million to Ease Traffic Woes It Helped Create', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car Services and Livery Cabs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Congestion Pricing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khosrowshahi, Dara', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matthiessen, Alex', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-26T17:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/308731e6-6c23-5b1f-bfa6-7c4288f8311a', 'word_count': 1003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/308731e6-6c23-5b1f-bfa6-7c4288f8311a'}, {'abstract': 'Making the batteries rechargeable and lowering their cost are seen as important advances in enabling the electric grid to depend on power from renewable sources. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/business/energy-environment/zinc-battery-explain.html', 'snippet': 'Making the batteries rechargeable and lowering their cost are seen as important advances in enabling the electric grid to depend on power from renewable sources. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past six years, 110 villages in Africa and Asia received their power from solar panels and batteries that use zinc and oxygen. The batteries are the basis of an innovative energy