ine': 'How Zinc Batteries Could Transform How Energy Is Stored', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Batteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lithium (Metal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zinc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soon-Shiong, Patrick', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NantEnergy Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-26T17:33:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ivan Penn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ivan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Penn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e8536c0-4a1e-5249-8a45-b2801dcdd27f', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e8536c0-4a1e-5249-8a45-b2801dcdd27f'}, {'abstract': 'Mary Gabriel moves from exalted art criticism to the seamiest gossip in her gratifying and generous group portrait of Lee Krasner, Elaine de Kooning, Grace Hartigan, Joan Mitchell and Helen Frankenthaler.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/books/review-ninth-street-women-mary-gabriel-lee-krasner-elaine-de-kooning-joan-mitchell.html', 'snippet': 'Mary Gabriel moves from exalted art criticism to the seamiest gossip in her gratifying and generous group portrait of Lee Krasner, Elaine de Kooning, Grace Hartigan, Joan Mitchell and Helen Frankenthaler.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mary Gabriel knows that the subjects of her new book would have probably bristled at its title and, consequently, the very foundation of her approach. While working on “Ninth Street Women: Lee Krasner, Elaine de Kooning, Grace Hartigan, Joan Mitchell, and Helen Frankenthaler: Five Painters and the Movement That Changed Modern Art,” Gabriel sensed the “irony of writing about these characters as ‘women artists,’” when they themselves refused “to be characterized as such.” As Elaine de Kooning put it in 1971, in a pointed rebuke to the budding field of feminist art history, “To be put in any category not defined by one’s work is to be falsified.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/books/27bookgabriel3/27bookgabriel3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/27/books/27bookgabriel3/27bookgabriel3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 745}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/books/27bookgabriel3/27bookgabriel3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 825, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/books/27bookgabriel3/27bookgabriel3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1650, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/books/27bookgabriel3/27bookgabriel3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/27/books/27bookgabriel3/27bookgabriel3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima