eld work, even though to do so as a married woman “was not heard of.” She became an expert on gender in the Caribbean.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/obituaries/constance-sutton-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Margaret Mead urged her to do field work, even though to do so as a married woman “was not heard of.” She became an expert on gender in the Caribbean.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1956, Constance Sutton, a recent master’s degree graduate of the University of Chicago, was hired by Margaret Mead, the pre-eminent anthropologist, to edit her latest book. Dr. Mead, who was teaching at Columbia University, was impressed by Ms. Sutton’s credentials but was baffled by one question: Why, after finishing all of her course work, hadn’t she gotten her doctorate?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/obituaries/27SUTTON1/27SUTTON1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 792, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/27/obituaries/27SUTTON1/27SUTTON1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 792}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/obituaries/27SUTTON1/27SUTTON1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 776, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/obituaries/27SUTTON1/27SUTTON1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1552, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/obituaries/27SUTTON1/27SUTTON1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/27/obituaries/27SUTTON1/27SUTTON1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/obituaries/27SUTTON1/27SUTTON1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Constance Sutton, Feminist Anthropologist, Is Dead at 92', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Constance Sutton, 92, Feminist Anthropologist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY AND ANTHROPOLOGY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caribbean Area', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sutton, Constance (1926-2018)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mead, Margaret', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-26T17:39:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a47b274c-da74-5604-9626-2f81f8daed3b', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a47b274c-da74-5604-9626-2f81f8daed3b'}, {'abstract': 'As Noah Cyrus, musical family royalty, seeks to find an identity, Bhad Bhabie, viral star, arrives at one naturally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/arts/music/bhad-bhabie-noah-cyrus-review.html', 'snippet': 'As Noah Cyrus, musical family royalty, seeks to find an identity, Bhad Bhabie, viral star, arrives at one naturally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The concerted effort to Make Noah Cyrus Happen began in earnest a year ago with the release of “Again,” an ill-advised and limp collaboration with the controversial rapper XXXTentacion. Like her sister Miley before her, Ms. Cyrus was aligning herself with hip-hop, though unlike Miley, she did not appear to be having any fun. That alliance was just one of several Ms. Cyrus struck — an incomplete list of collaborators includes dance music producers (Marshmello and Matoma), pop singers (MØ), rappers (Lil Xan) and R&B singers (Gallant, Labrinth) — with Ms. Cyrus adjusting as needed to the circumstance.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/arts/27bhadcyrus4/merlin_135521235_881da744-5925-4e26-9a33-55b83f97f688-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/27/arts/27bhadcyrus4/merlin_135521235_881da744-5925-4e26-9a33-55b83f97f688-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/arts/27bhadcyrus4/merlin_135521235_881da744-5925-4e26-9a33-55b83f97f688-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/arts/27bhadcyrus4/merlin_135521235_881da744-5925-4e26-9a33-55b83f97f688-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1387, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/arts/27bhadcyrus4/27bhadcyrus4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/27/arts/27bhadcyrus4/27bhadcyrus4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/arts/27bhadcyrus4/27bhadcyrus4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bhad Bhabie and Noah Cyrus, Invented From the Ground Up', 'kicker': 'Album Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Both Are Inventions. Only One Seems at Ease.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cyrus, Noah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Good Cry (Album)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bregoli, Danielle (Bhad Bhabie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': '15 (Album)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-26T17:47:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a21c900-94f0-5679-aaf5-6f8361ee7856', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a21c900-94f0-5679-aaf5-6f8361ee7856'}, {'abstract': 'This week world leaders are meeting in New York, and climate change is on the agenda. And, meet the intrepid photographer behind our recent story from Greenland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/climate/climate-week-and-photo-stories.html', 'snippet': 'This week world leaders are meeting in New York, and climate change is on the agenda. And, meet the intrepid photographer behind our recent story from Greenland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to the Climate Fwd: newsletter. The New York Times climate team emails readers once a week with stories and insights about climate change. Sign up here to get it in your inbox.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/26/climate/26cli-newsletter-cliweek/26cli-newsletter-cliweek-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/26/climate/26cli-newsletter-cliweek/26cli-newsletter-cliweek-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/26/climate/26cli-newsletter-cliweek/26cli-newsletter-cliweek-jumbo.gif', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/26/climate/26cli-newsletter-cliweek/26cli-newsletter-cliweek-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/26/climate/26cli-newsletter-cliweek/26cli-newsletter-cliweek-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/26/climate/26cli-newsletter-cliweek/26cli-newsletter-cliweek-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'ra