://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/26/dining/australia-salad-sandwich.html', 'snippet': 'The once-ubiquitous lunch item’s prominence has dwindled, and it deserves more respect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some foods are so ordinary and ubiquitous that we fail to even notice them. This seems especially true in Australia when it comes to our more plebeian offerings. Some, admittedly, become iconic, like the meat pie or Vegemite. But while American food writing celebrates the tater tot, ranch dressing and Hot Pockets, Australia lets many edible components of its collective childhood slip by, unsung and unexamined.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/03/autossell/03Fare2/merlin_144252351_52aa8ced-8bb0-484a-98d9-cdf71cb7f8c7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/10/03/autossell/03Fare2/merlin_144252351_52aa8ced-8bb0-484a-98d9-cdf71cb7f8c7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 774}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/03/autossell/03Fare2/merlin_144252351_52aa8ced-8bb0-484a-98d9-cdf71cb7f8c7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 794, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/03/autossell/03Fare2/merlin_144252351_52aa8ced-8bb0-484a-98d9-cdf71cb7f8c7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1588, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/03/autossell/03Fare2/03Fare2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/10/03/autossell/03Fare2/03Fare2-thumbSt