umbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/27/world/27USBriefing-amcore/27USBriefing-Kavanaugh-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brett Kavanaugh, China, Octopus: Your Thursday Briefing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-09-27T09:44:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Stanford and Jillian Rayfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jillian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rayfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/b23f4efa-b936-5af7-a8f9-70b4b43f7e20', 'word_count': 1420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b23f4efa-b936-5af7-a8f9-70b4b43f7e20'}, {'abstract': 'It is almost unthinkable that there will be a second Supreme Court justice taking his seat under suspicions of perjury and sexual misconduct. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/27/opinion/kavanaugh-christine-blasey-ford-hearing.html', 'snippet': 'It is almost unthinkable that there will be a second Supreme Court justice taking his seat under suspicions of perjury and sexual misconduct. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a reason Thursday’s Senate Judiciary Committee hearing will be short and feature only two witnesses, the Supreme Court nominee Judge Brett Kavanaugh and his accuser Christine Blasey Ford. Republicans have designed the hearing to end in a “he said, she said” stalemate. No matter how credible Dr. Blasey is, isolating her as a lone accuser is the most effective political strategy for confirming Judge Ka