 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crenshaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd84cace-fce0-5f6b-92ce-a77c43fb41ac', 'word_count': 1529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd84cace-fce0-5f6b-92ce-a77c43fb41ac'}, {'abstract': 'Thomas Ostermeier and Krystian Lupa present works at the city’s major playhouses at the beginning of a new theater season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/27/theater/thomas-ostermeier-comedie-franciase-krystian-lupa-odeon.html', 'snippet': 'Thomas Ostermeier and Krystian Lupa present works at the city’s major playhouses at the beginning of a new theater season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — On paper, the theater directors Krystian Lupa and Thomas Ostermeier have much in common. They are heavyweights of the European stage: Mr. Ostermeier is the director of the famous Schaubühne theater in Berlin, while Mr. Lupa’s productions have long been revered beyond his native Poland. Both are renowned for their pin-sharp direction of actors as well as their willingness to tackle onstage the rise of extremist forces.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28paristheater01-inyt/merlin_144253395_f3547bd9-b158-42a0-b461-dd65a46e2536-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28paristheater01-inyt/merlin_144253395_f3547bd9-b158-42a0-b461-dd65a46e2536-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28paristheater01-inyt/merlin_144253395_f3547bd9-b158-42a0-b461-dd65a46e2536-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':