umbnail': 'images/2018/07/12/world/12dc-scotus-inyt/merlin_141045930_be34e2dc-b23a-494d-8e12-9664f8068b99-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/07/12/world/12dc-scotus-inyt/merlin_141045930_be34e2dc-b23a-494d-8e12-9664f8068b99-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Readers Want to Ask Kavanaugh', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Christine Blasey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kavanaugh, Brett M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-27T15:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel L. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c55d5f29-9f4f-5c18-bd15-03b5c90bd9f7', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c55d5f29-9f4f-5c18-bd15-03b5c90bd9f7'}, {'abstract': 'The movie’s meanspirited humor is out of place with the perky conventionality of its film style.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/27/movies/summer-03-review.html', 'snippet': 'The movie’s meanspirited humor is out of place with the perky conventionality of its film style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Jamie (Joey King) enters the pivotal summer of her adolescence in the far-off past of sunny 2003, she is a jaded teenager whose fantasies of love and sex have yet to be tested by experience. The death of her grandmother, Dotty (June Squibb), puts weekend keggers and girlish gossip on pause, but unexpectedly for Jamie, Dotty authorizes a teenage rebellion. Her final words of wisdom ring coarse and clear: Abandon your mother’s Judaism, and learn the secrets of oral sex.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28summerothree2/28summerothree2-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28summerothree2/28summerothree2-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28summerothree2/28summerothree2-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28summerothree2/28summerothree2-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 971, 'width': 1544, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28summerothree2/28summerothree2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28summerothree2/28summerothree2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28summerothree2/28summerothree2-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Summer ’03,’ Coming of Age Is More Bitter Than Sweet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Summer ’03', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Summer '03 (Movie)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Joey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gleason, Becca', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-27T15:01:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teo Bugbee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bugbee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/82780764-ed93-58d0-832c-509a0484e78a', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82780764-ed93-58d0-832c-509a0484e78a'}, {'abstract': 'The Bedlam show, stitched together from parts borrowed from Chekhov and Shakespeare, should perhaps be credited to Chekspeare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/27/theater/uncle-romeo-vanya-juliet-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Bedlam show, stitched together from parts borrowed from Chekhov and Shakespeare, should perhaps be credited to Chekspeare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the early 2000s, mash-ups had a cultural moment. Mad studio scientists would combine two (and sometimes more) completely different songs to create a new one. The trend peaked with Danger Mouse’s full-length “The Grey Album,” which fused the Beatles’ White Album with Jay-Z’s “The Black Album.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28uncleromeovanyajuliet1/merlin_144098025_a45b133b-3450-415d-90c7-adbbb44c7a96-articleLarge.jpg', 'height'