mselves, the industry is dreaming up new ways to keep drivers’ eyes on the road.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/27/business/distracted-driving-auto-industry.html', 'snippet': 'While people will always find a way to distract themselves, the industry is dreaming up new ways to keep drivers’ eyes on the road.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The large rubber strip that I was speeding toward on the Ventura Freeway near Los Angeles looked easy enough to avoid. I swerved, but not enough.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/business/28wheels-print/28Wheels-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/28/business/28wheels-print/28Wheels-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/business/28wheels-print/28Wheels-jumbo.gif', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/business/28wheels-print/28Wheels-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/business/28wheels-print/28Wheels-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/28/business/28wheels-print/28Wheels-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/business/28wheels-print/merlin_144430254_554a0642-3c00-4930-b209-3fa1792213bd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '2-Second Rule for Distracted Driving Can Mean Life or Death', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Challenge to Designers: Keep Drivers Focused', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Driver Distraction and Fatigue', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-27T21:07:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric A. Taub', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Taub', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f51a1b8a-4706-5837-aa55-442f8d303839', 'word_count': 1314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f51a1b8a-4706-5837-aa55-442f8d303839'}, {'abstract': 'Two shows attempt to bridge the rift in a museum’s mission: to honor its Barrio roots — and reach a global audience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/27/arts/design/el-museo-del-barrio-liliana-porter-review.html', 'snippet': 'Two shows attempt to bridge the rift in a museum’s mission: to honor its Barrio roots — and reach a global audience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Location, location, location. In real estate, place determines value. Sometimes it can for art too. El Museo  del Barrio originated in 1969 in classrooms, storefronts and a repurposed fire station in what was then the predominantly Puerto Rican neighborhood of East Harlem. The museum was a product of pride and necessity. In local public schools, young artist-activists, often working free, taught children the virtues of cultural self-expression and communal self-sufficiency. And they taught from experience. At the time, no mainstream art institution in the city would show their art. They needed a museum of their own and, collectively, they created one.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28elmuseo3/merlin_144314004_041cd4d0-7423-4f5b-b62d-f8d2bfcfb20a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28elmuseo3/merlin_144314004_041cd4d0-7423-4f5b-b62d-f8d2bfcfb20a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28elmuseo3/merlin_144314004_041cd4d0-7423-4f5b-b62d-f8d2bfcfb20a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28elmuseo3/merlin_144314004_041cd4d0-7423-4f5b-b62d-f8d2bfcfb20a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1629, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28elmuseo3/28elmuseo3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28elmuseo3/28elmuseo3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/28/arts/28elmuseo3/28elmuseo3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline':