lways with their own interests first. Trump could learn something.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — In his declared intention to “Make America Great Again,” President Trump appears set on destroying the foundations of American greatness. The multinational organizations and agreements that established peace and stability, and encouraged economic growth for some seven decades, were designed principally by Americans. They organized the world pretty much the way that suited them, and they reaped the benefits of dominating it through a complex network of organizations and treaties. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/opinion/28konstandaras/28konstandaras-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 478, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/10/01/opinion/28konstandaras/28konstandaras-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 478}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/opinion/28konstandaras/28konstandaras-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 816, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/opinion/28konstandaras/28konstandaras-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1116, 'width': 1400, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/opinion/28konstandaras/28konstandaras-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/10/01/opinion/28konstandaras/28konstandaras-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/opinion/28konstandaras/28konstandaras-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Alliances Made Athens Great', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thucydides (460-395 BC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Athens (Greece)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-28T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikos Konstandaras', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikos', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Konstandaras', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4693dd9-04d9-5311-bc5f-274acc61aa93', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4693dd9-04d9-5311-bc5f-274acc61aa93'}, {'abstract': 'At age 29, McIlroy is trying hard to make his life more than just an extension of the golf course. He seems to be succeeding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/28/sports/golf/golf-ryder-cup-mcilroy.html', 'snippet': 'At age 29, McIlroy is trying hard to make his life more than just an extension of the golf course. He seems to be succeeding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST.-QUENTIN-EN-YVELINES, France — Rory McIlroy is straddling two continents, two tours and two colliding worlds — the celebrity and the secular. It is a lot to bala