, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f93b0849-2c3f-5d33-b164-78a23735d197', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f93b0849-2c3f-5d33-b164-78a23735d197'}, {'abstract': 'When water replaces air in a fabric, the material itself reflects less light. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/28/science/how-wet-clothes-become-translucent.html', 'snippet': 'When water replaces air in a fabric, the material itself reflects less light. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'A. Cloth, like paper, is made up of discrete strands of fiber with air between them. Light hitting the dry material is somewhat scattered within it, but a good share is reflected to the eye. This renders the material visible.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/02/science/02QNACLOTHRAIN/merlin_144428133_cf1af468-d06b-4818-a05e-f86428cfe3fe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/10/02/science/02QNACLOTHRAIN/merlin_144428133_cf1af468-d06b-4818-a05e-f86428cfe3fe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 639}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/02/science/02QNACLOTHRAIN/merlin_144428133_cf1af468-d06b-4818-a05e-f86428cfe3fe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 962, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/02/science/02QNACLOTHRAIN/merlin_144428133_cf1af468-d06b-4818-a05e-f86428cfe3fe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1597, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/02/science/