Large', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Delicate Treatment for a Just-as-Delicate Fish', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Delicate Treatment to Match the Fish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Butter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-28T15:45:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/528725ec-7bd2-5268-8070-fc96a99b2e61', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/528725ec-7bd2-5268-8070-fc96a99b2e61'}, {'abstract': 'With the photo app’s founders gone, Facebook is likely to change it significantly. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/28/opinion/instagram-facebook.html', 'snippet': 'With the photo app’s founders gone, Facebook is likely to change it significantly. ', 'lead_paragraph': "On the face of it, there’s nothing surprising about Instagram's founders leaving six years after the company was sold. Mike Krieger and Kevin Systrom’s tenures at Facebook were longer than that of most Facebook employees, where the average is 2.5 years. And Instagram has come a long way since Facebook bought it in April 2012 for a reported $1 billion. In the past six years, Instagram has grown from 50 million users to more than a billion users, and it currently employs more than 700 people. Today, its estimated worth is over $100 billion. ", 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '