': 'A third-generation diabetic herself, she upset conventional wisdom in finding that women whose blood sugar level was controlled could safely give birth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Lois Jovanovic, who redeemed a childhood pledge when she pioneered a medical procedure that enabled more women with diabetes to deliver healthy babies, died on Sept. 18 at her home in Santa Barbara, Calif. She was 71 and had herself been treated for diabetes since giving birth decades ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/obituaries/30JOVANOVIC-OBIT/merlin_144430902_973f48be-c311-4cd2-a99c-84c864aff034-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/30/obituaries/30JOVANOVIC-OBIT/merlin_144430902_973f48be-c311-4cd2-a99c-84c864aff034-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/obituaries/30JOVANOVIC-OBIT/merlin_144430902_973f48be-c311-4cd2-a99c-84c864aff034-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/obituaries/30JOVANOVIC-OBIT/merlin_144430902_973f48be-c311-4cd2-a99c-84c864aff034-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/obituaries/30JOVANOVIC-OBIT/28JOVANOVIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/30/obituaries/30JOVANOVIC-OBIT/28JOVANOVIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumb