partment in Manhattan from a family friend. On move-in day, we noticed some broken or damaged items, and immediately requested repairs. Over the past few weeks, they fixed everything (with some prodding), except for a broken outlet in my roommate’s bedroom. Rather than fix it, the owners suggested we use a power strip with a different outlet. But the only other outlet in the room is behind a heavy dresser, and we’ve been told not to move the furniture. Do we have grounds to demand they fix it?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/realestate/30ASK/merlin_144364407_baa2f92c-7530-4926-9fb8-c38fcb6f9f88-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 118, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/30/realestate/30ASK/merlin_144364407_baa2f92c-7530-4926-9fb8-c38fcb6f9f88-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 118}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/realestate/30ASK/merlin_144364407_baa2f92c-7530-4926-9fb8-c38fcb6f9f88-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 201, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/realestate/30ASK/merlin_144364407_baa2f92c-7530-4926-9fb8-c38fcb6f9f88-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 1680, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/realestate/30ASK/merlin_144364407_baa2f92c-7530-4926-9fb8-c38fcb6f9f88-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/30/realestate/30ASK/merlin_144364407_baa2f92c-7530-4926-9fb