t has faced far greater challenges before. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'On my first day as United States ambassador in Prague in 2011, I found, branded beneath the surface of an antique table in my official residence, a small black swastika. It was one of many swastikas hidden throughout the palace, relics of the days when it was occupied by the Nazis.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/opinion/sunday/30Eisen/merlin_114973781_884e1993-bfdd-4509-b043-b50d811c2f2f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/30/opinion/sunday/30Eisen/merlin_114973781_884e1993-bfdd-4509-b043-b50d811c2f2f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/opinion/sunday/30Eisen/merlin_114973781_884e1993-bfdd-4509-b043-b50d811c2f2f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/opinion/sunday/30Eisen/merlin_114973781_884e1993-bfdd-4509-b043-b50d811c2f2f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/opinion/sunday/30Eisen/30Eisen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/30/opinion/sunday/30Eisen/30Eisen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/30/opinion/sunday/30Eisen/30Eisen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Depressed About the Future of Democracy? Study History ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A History Lesson in Optimism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-29T18:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Norman Eisen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Norman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eisen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c376fde3-8f93-598c-bf07-d6946a82ee6b', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c376fde3-8f93-598c-bf07-d6946a82ee6b'}, {'abstract': 'Reality TV has always been the guidebook for this presidency. And most popular series last for six seasons. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/29/sunday-review/trump-2020-reality-tv.html', 'snippet': 'Reality TV has always been the guidebook for this presidency. And most popular series last for six seasons. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mike Fleiss, the creator of “The Bachelor” and “Who Wants to Marry a Multimillionaire?” helped pioneer reality television in the early 2000s, he quickly realized that for any show to work, the audience needed to feel invested. “Whenever you’re developing one of these shows, you have to find stakes — true love or a million dollars,” Mr. Fleiss said.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_p