_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/159d1b97-ac3c-50b2-acd7-c668bf8d76fb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/159d1b97-ac3c-50b2-acd7-c668bf8d76fb'}, {'abstract': 'Two Harlem churches have buildings that have deteriorated. They also own nearby brownstones or vacant lots. Now they are debating whether to sell some of their real estate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/30/nyregion/harlem-church-nyc-.html', 'snippet': 'Two Harlem churches have buildings that have deteriorated. They also own nearby brownstones or vacant lots. Now they are debating whether to sell some of their real estate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a tower above Malcolm X Boulevard in Harlem are more than 40 large bells that were fabricated in the Netherlands — they form the carillon of a once-proud church, St. Martin’s, and are one of only three carillons in New York City. The queen mother of the Netherlands attended a dedication ceremony in the 1950s. The current Episcopal bishop of New York says it was “a giant big deal” that she was there.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/nyregion/01grace/01grace-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/10/01/nyregion/01grace/01grace-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/nyregion/01grace/01grace-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/nyregion/01grace/01grace-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/nyregion/01grace/01grace-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/10/01/nyregion/01grace/01grace-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/nyregion/01grace/01grace-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bells of St. Martin’s Fall Silent as Churches in Harlem Struggle', 'kicker': 'Grace Notes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Attendance Is Lagging, but the Property Values Are Soaring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Churches (Buildings)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-30T14:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/096202e9-b28d-5891-8edb-bd3c28f0c21f', 'word_count': 1474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/096202e9-b28d-5891-8edb-bd3c28f0c21f'}, {'abstract': 'A new box set makes the case that the pioneering female stand-up should be considered in the same class as David Letterman and Andy Kaufman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/30/arts/television/elayne-boosler-the-comedy-master-who-hasnt-gotten-her-due.html', 'snippet': 'A new box set makes the case that the pioneering female stand-up should be considered in the same class as David Letterman and Andy Kaufman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In books, TV series and documentaries, stand-up comics of the 1970s have become nearly as mythologized as the auteurs of the New Hollywood. If Richard Pryor, David Letterman and Andy Kaufman were the Martin Scorsese, Steven Spielberg and Francis Ford Coppola of the club scene, then Elayne Boosler is the Hal Ashby, the misunderstood master who never got proper due.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/arts/01elayne-boosler1/merlin_144489624_142d0524-4ab9-4fc2-aed2-2d8a0be89161-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/10/01/arts/01elayne-boosler1/merlin_144489624_142d0524-4ab9-4fc2-aed2-2d8a0be89161-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/arts/01elayne-boosler1/merlin_144489624_142d0524-4ab9-4fc2-aed2-2d8a0be89161-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 641, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/arts/01elayne-boosler1/merlin_144489624_142d0524-4ab9-4fc2-aed2-2d8a0be89161-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1018, 'width': 1626, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/arts/01elayne-boosler1/merlin_144489624_142d0524-4ab9-4fc2-aed2-2d8a0be89161-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/10/01/arts/01elayne-boosler1/merlin_144489624_142d0524-4ab9-4fc2-aed2-2d8a0be89161-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/01/arts/01elayne-boosler1/merlin_144489624_142d0524-4ab9-4fc2-aed2-2d8a0be89161-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Comedy Master Who Hasn’t Gotten Her Due: Elayne Boosler', 'kicker': 'On Comedy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Master Not Yet Given Her Due', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boosler, Elayne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-09-30T14:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a73d1612-1d2f-5b85-8c91-94af24e109f8', 'word_count': 1012, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a73d1612-1d2f-5b85-8c91-94af24e109f8'}, {'abstract': 'Start this week off with a Sunday roast before ending it stunningly, with a beer-can chicken.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/30/dining/what-to-cook-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Start this week off with a Sunday roast before ending it stunningly, with a beer-can chicken.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. I am sorry to be this guy today, coming in hot on a Sunday morning when maybe all you’d like to be doing is spacing out or reading the new Robert Galbraith novel from J.K. Rowling. But really, today is the day to deep-clean your fridge after a summer of berries and ribs, endless new cheeses for August soirees, kombucha spills and leaking containers of sambal oelek and maple syrup. Look and see: three bottles of ketchup; two of mayonnaise; two of pickled jalapeño. When did you buy that sour cream? Are those … radishes in the back of the crisper?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/dining/15COOKING-BEERCAN-CHICKEN3/15COOKING-BEERCAN-CHICKEN3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/15/dining/15COOKING-BEERCAN-CHICKEN3/15COOKING-BEERCAN-CHICKEN3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/dining/15COOKING-BEERCAN-CHICKEN3/15COOKING-BEERCAN-CHICKEN3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/dining/15COOKING-BEERCAN-CHICKEN3/15COOKING-BEERCAN-CHICKEN3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/dining/15COOKING-BEERCAN-CHICKEN3/15COOKING-BEERCAN-CHICKEN3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/15/dining/15COOKING-BEERCAN-CHICKEN3/15COOKING-BEERCAN-CHICKEN3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/dining/15COOKING-BEERCAN-CHICKEN3/15COOK